{"repo": "pypa/pipenv", "pull_number": 6773, "instance_id": "pypa__pipenv-6773", "issue_numbers": ["6109"], "base_commit": "bb002cd7340ffe22a917acd69f820fcaedcd7caa", "patch": "diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yaml b/.github/workflows/ci.yaml\nindex 2baf992739..e3fea0f789 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yaml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yaml\n@@ -285,13 +285,13 @@ jobs:\n     needs: [lint]\n     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n     timeout-minutes: 30\n-    # The pure-python backend is experimental; report its numbers without\n-    # letting a failure there block CI.\n+    # The pure-python and uv backends are experimental; report their\n+    # numbers without letting a failure there block CI.\n     continue-on-error: ${{ matrix.backend != 'pip' }}\n     strategy:\n       fail-fast: false\n       matrix:\n-        backend: [pip, pure-python]\n+        backend: [pip, pure-python, uv]\n     steps:\n       - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n       - uses: actions/setup-python@v6\n@@ -303,6 +303,9 @@ jobs:\n           sudo apt-get install -y libxmlsec1-dev librdkafka-dev\n       - name: Install benchmark utilities\n         run: pip install csv2md\n+      - name: Install uv\n+        if: matrix.backend == 'uv'\n+        run: pip install uv\n       - name: Run benchmark suite\n         working-directory: benchmarks\n         run: python benchmark.py --backend ${{ matrix.backend }}\ndiff --git a/benchmarks/README.md b/benchmarks/README.md\nindex abca76e4b0..a2f5ba9d56 100644\n--- a/benchmarks/README.md\n+++ b/benchmarks/README.md\n@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@ python benchmark.py stats              # Generate stats.csv\n # Benchmark the experimental pure-Python resolver backend\n python benchmark.py --backend pure-python\n \n+# Benchmark the uv resolver backend (requires uv on $PATH; cold runs\n+# also clear uv's cache)\n+python benchmark.py --backend uv\n+\n # Local diagnosis helpers\n python benchmark.py lock-warm --repeat 3\n python benchmark.py lock-warm --profile\n@@ -53,7 +57,7 @@ python benchmark.py update-warm --output-json update-results.json\n \n ### CI Integration\n \n-The benchmarks run automatically in GitHub Actions on the `ubuntu-latest` runner as part of the CI pipeline, once per resolver backend (`pip` and `pure-python`). The `pure-python` job is non-blocking while that backend is experimental. Results are:\n+The benchmarks run automatically in GitHub Actions on the `ubuntu-latest` runner as part of the CI pipeline, once per resolver backend (`pip`, `pure-python` and `uv`). The `pure-python` and `uv` jobs are non-blocking while those backends are experimental. Results are:\n \n - Displayed in the job summary with timing statistics, one table per backend\n - Uploaded as `pipenv-benchmark-stats-<backend>` artifacts for historical analysis\ndiff --git a/benchmarks/benchmark.py b/benchmarks/benchmark.py\nindex a578fdc78d..737911bce1 100644\n--- a/benchmarks/benchmark.py\n+++ b/benchmarks/benchmark.py\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@\n     \"stats\",\n )\n \n-BACKENDS = (\"pip\", \"pure-python\")\n+BACKENDS = (\"pip\", \"pure-python\", \"uv\")\n DEFAULT_BACKEND = \"pip\"\n \n TIMED_STATS = (\n@@ -436,7 +436,7 @@ def tool_label(self) -> str:\n         return f\"pipenv ({self.backend})\"\n \n     def clean_cache(self):\n-        \"\"\"Clean pipenv and pip caches.\"\"\"\n+        \"\"\"Clean pipenv and pip caches, plus uv's when benchmarking uv.\"\"\"\n         print(\"Cleaning caches...\")\n         cache_dirs = [Path.home() / \".cache\" / \"pip\", Path.home() / \".cache\" / \"pipenv\"]\n \n@@ -444,6 +444,17 @@ def clean_cache(self):\n             if cache_dir.exists():\n                 shutil.rmtree(cache_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n \n+        # The uv backend resolves through uv's own cache; leaving it warm\n+        # would make the \"cold\" timings meaningless.\n+        if self.backend == \"uv\":\n+            subprocess.run(\n+                [\"uv\", \"cache\", \"clean\"],\n+                capture_output=True,\n+                check=False,\n+                timeout=300,\n+                env=subprocess_env(),\n+            )\n+\n     def clean_venv(self):\n         \"\"\"Clean virtual environment.\"\"\"\n         print(\"Cleaning virtual environment...\")\ndiff --git a/docs/index.md b/docs/index.md\nindex b029f9ca07..5a92ffe0f8 100644\n--- a/docs/index.md\n+++ b/docs/index.md\n@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@ security\n troubleshooting\n specifiers\n indexes\n+resolver_backends\n credentials\n shell\n docker\ndiff --git a/docs/resolver_backends.md b/docs/resolver_backends.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..60d2280c45\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/resolver_backends.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@\n+# Resolver Backends\n+\n+Pipenv resolves your `Pipfile` into a `Pipfile.lock` using a pluggable resolver backend. The backend decides *how* dependencies are resolved; the lockfile it produces has the same format whichever backend you use.\n+\n+| Backend | Description |\n+|---------|-------------|\n+| `pip` | The default. Pipenv's vendored, patched copy of pip's resolver. |\n+| `pure-python` | An in-tree resolver that reads index metadata directly. |\n+| `uv` | Delegates resolution to [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), a fast resolver written in Rust. Requires `uv` on your `$PATH`. |\n+\n+## Selecting a Backend\n+\n+In order of precedence:\n+\n+1. A command-line option: `--backend` on `pipenv lock`, or `--resolver` on any command that locks (`install`, `update`, `upgrade`, `uninstall`, `lock`):\n+\n+   ```bash\n+   $ pipenv lock --backend uv\n+   $ pipenv install requests --resolver uv\n+   ```\n+\n+2. The `PIPENV_RESOLVER` environment variable:\n+\n+   ```bash\n+   $ PIPENV_RESOLVER=uv pipenv lock\n+   ```\n+\n+3. The `resolver_backend` setting in the `[pipenv]` section of your `Pipfile`, which applies to everyone working on the project:\n+\n+   ```toml\n+   [pipenv]\n+   resolver_backend = \"uv\"\n+   ```\n+\n+If none of these is set, the `pip` backend is used.\n+\n+## The uv Backend\n+\n+### Installing uv\n+\n+Pipenv does not bundle uv. Install it with any of:\n+\n+```bash\n+$ pip install uv\n+$ pipx install uv\n+$ curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\n+```\n+\n+If the `uv` backend is selected and `uv` is not on your `$PATH`, locking fails with an error explaining how to install it. Pipenv never silently falls back to another backend.\n+\n+### What It Does\n+\n+The `uv` backend resolves with `uv pip compile` against your project's virtualenv interpreter, so it targets the same single environment the `pip` backend does (including the `python_full_version` from `[requires]`). It keeps Pipenv's semantics:\n+\n+- **Index restriction.** A package without an `index` key resolves only from the first `[[source]]`. A package with `index = \"name\"` resolves only from that source. Other sources are never searched implicitly, which protects against dependency-confusion attacks. This also applies when a category depends on a package pinned to an index in another category. To guarantee that, such a package takes part in resolving every non-default category, even one that turns out not to need it, and is left out of that category's lock section in that case.\n+- **Hashes.** Every distribution of each pinned version is hashed, so the lockfile installs on other platforms.\n+- **Markers.** Markers on `Pipfile` entries are kept and carried over to the dependencies those packages introduce. A package whose markers exclude the current platform is still recorded in the lockfile.\n+- **Categories.** Non-default categories such as `[dev-packages]` are resolved consistently with the versions locked for `[packages]`.\n+- **Credentials.** Credentials in source URLs, `.netrc` files, and `PIPENV_KEYRING_PROVIDER` work as they do with the `pip` backend.\n+\n+Installation (`pipenv install`, `pipenv sync`) still uses pip, whichever backend produced the lockfile.\n+\n+### Differences From the pip Backend\n+\n+The `uv` backend picks the same versions as the `pip` backend in the vast majority of projects, but the lockfiles are not always byte-for-byte identical:\n+\n+- The `pip` backend adds each package's `Requires-Python` to its `markers` (for example `python_version >= '3.9'`). The `uv` backend does not. These markers are always true for the environment the lockfile was created for.\n+- For a direct `file` URL dependency, the `uv` backend records only the hash of that file.\n+- Options passed with `--extra-pip-args` are ignored, with a warning.\n+\n+Switching backends on an existing project can therefore produce a small lockfile diff on the next `pipenv lock`.\ndiff --git a/news/6109.feature.rst b/news/6109.feature.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..e68beb4727\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/6109.feature.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+Add a ``uv`` resolver backend. ``pipenv lock --backend uv``, ``PIPENV_RESOLVER=uv`` or ``resolver_backend = \"uv\"`` in the ``[pipenv]`` section of the ``Pipfile`` resolves dependencies with `uv <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/>`_ (which must be on ``$PATH``) while keeping pipenv's index restriction, hashes and markers. See the new \"Resolver Backends\" documentation page.\ndiff --git a/pipenv/cli/options.py b/pipenv/cli/options.py\nindex 2e63810dea..f6b3237cad 100644\n--- a/pipenv/cli/options.py\n+++ b/pipenv/cli/options.py\n@@ -347,7 +347,7 @@ def _add_backend_option(p):\n \n     User-facing surface for the pluggable resolver-backend dispatcher.\n     ``--backend NAME`` is the documented spelling on ``pipenv lock``;\n-    accepted values are ``pip`` (default) and ``pure-python``.  Unlike\n+    accepted values are ``pip`` (default), ``pure-python`` and ``uv``.  Unlike\n     ``--resolver NAME`` (kept for back-compat with T_F.5 scaffolding),\n     this flag validates the value at parse time via ``choices=`` so\n     typos fail with an actionable error instead of falling through to\n@@ -362,7 +362,7 @@ def _add_backend_option(p):\n     p.add_argument(\n         \"--backend\",\n         dest=\"backend\",\n-        choices=(\"pip\", \"pure-python\"),\n+        choices=(\"pip\", \"pure-python\", \"uv\"),\n         default=None,\n         help=(\n             \"Resolver backend to use.  Defaults to \"\ndiff --git a/pipenv/resolver/backends/__init__.py b/pipenv/resolver/backends/__init__.py\nindex 73e4aac656..aa935504c7 100644\n--- a/pipenv/resolver/backends/__init__.py\n+++ b/pipenv/resolver/backends/__init__.py\n@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@\n from pipenv.resolver.backends.base import REGISTRY, Backend\n from pipenv.resolver.backends.pip import PipBackend\n from pipenv.resolver.backends.pure_python import PurePythonBackend\n+from pipenv.resolver.backends.uv import UvBackend\n \n # Default backend used when no explicit selection has been made via CLI,\n # env var, or Pipfile.  Kept at module scope so the dispatcher in\n@@ -36,6 +37,9 @@\n # ``None``); the dispatcher injects cache/fetcher/session/metadata_cache\n # before invoking ``.resolve()`` (Phase 4 wiring).\n REGISTRY[\"pure-python\"] = PurePythonBackend\n+# gh-6109: the uv backend shells out to a system ``uv`` binary; its\n+# ``is_available()`` gates dispatch so a missing binary fails loud.\n+REGISTRY[\"uv\"] = UvBackend\n \n \n def get_backend(name: str) -> Backend:\n@@ -89,6 +93,7 @@ def list_backends() -> list[str]:\n     \"PipBackend\",\n     \"PurePythonBackend\",\n     \"REGISTRY\",\n+    \"UvBackend\",\n     \"get_backend\",\n     \"list_backends\",\n ]\ndiff --git a/pipenv/resolver/backends/uv.py b/pipenv/resolver/backends/uv.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..64b910c987\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pipenv/resolver/backends/uv.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,870 @@\n+\"\"\"``uv`` resolver backend (gh-6109).\n+\n+Implements the Initiative F ``Backend`` protocol by shelling out to\n+``uv pip compile``.  uv is **not** vendored: the backend discovers the\n+``uv`` binary on ``$PATH`` and the dispatcher fails loud (with an\n+install hint) when it is missing \u2014 see the maintainer sign-off in\n+``docs/dev/initiative-f-backends-design.md`` (answers 4 and 8).\n+\n+Why ``uv pip compile`` rather than ``uv lock``\n+----------------------------------------------\n+The pip backend resolves for a *single* target environment (the\n+project's interpreter, optionally with the Pipfile's\n+``python_full_version`` patched into the marker environment).\n+``uv lock`` performs a *universal* resolution that may fork a package\n+into several versions under different markers, which ``Pipfile.lock``\n+(one version per package) cannot represent.  ``uv pip compile`` with\n+``--python <interpreter>`` resolves for the same single environment the\n+pip backend targets, and ``--generate-hashes`` records hashes for every\n+distribution of the pinned version \u2014 the same coverage the pip\n+backend's hash collection produces, so the lockfile installs on other\n+platforms.\n+\n+Flow inside :meth:`UvBackend.resolve`:\n+\n+1. Translate ``request.packages.specs`` (pip-install argument lines)\n+   into PEP 508 dependencies, ``[tool.uv.sources]`` pins and path\n+   sources, and write them to a throwaway ``pyproject.toml``.\n+2. Make the first source uv's default index and every other source an\n+   ``explicit = true`` ``[[tool.uv.index]]`` entry, consulted only for\n+   packages pinned to it.  This is pipenv's index-restriction security\n+   property: an unpinned package resolves *only* from the primary\n+   index.  ``uv pip compile`` ignores ``default = true`` on indexes\n+   declared in the input file, so the primary index is passed as\n+   ``UV_DEFAULT_INDEX`` \u2014 in the environment rather than on the command\n+   line, so credentials embedded in the URL stay out of process\n+   listings.  uv only honours an index pin on a requirement it is\n+   resolving, so a package pinned in another Pipfile category is added\n+   as a requirement too, and dropped from the result afterwards if\n+   nothing in this category needs it.\n+3. Write ``request.resolved_default_deps`` as a constraints file.\n+4. Run ``uv pip compile`` and parse its requirements-format output\n+   (``--hash`` lines and ``# via`` annotations).\n+5. Translate each entry into a :class:`LockedRequirement`.  Markers of\n+   marker-guarded top-level packages are folded onto the transitive\n+   dependencies only they introduce.\n+\n+Known difference from the pip backend: the pip backend AND-merges each\n+package's ``Requires-Python`` into its ``markers``; uv does not report\n+``Requires-Python``, so those markers are absent.  They are always true\n+for the environment the lockfile was resolved for.\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import json\n+import os\n+import re\n+import shutil\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+import tempfile\n+import time\n+import traceback\n+from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Any, Mapping, Sequence\n+from urllib.parse import unquote, urlsplit, urlunsplit\n+\n+from pipenv.resolver.schema import (\n+    SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+    Diagnostics,\n+    InternalError,\n+    LockedRequirement,\n+    ResolutionError,\n+    ResolverRequest,\n+    ResolverResponse,\n+    ResolverSuccess,\n+    Source,\n+    VCSPin,\n+)\n+\n+# Name of the throwaway project uv compiles.  uv reports it in\n+# ``# via`` annotations for top-level requirements.\n+_ROOT_PROJECT = \"your-pipfile\"\n+\n+_DEFAULT_SOURCE = Source(name=\"pypi\", url=\"https://pypi.org/simple\")\n+\n+_VCS_SCHEMES = (\"git\", \"hg\", \"svn\", \"bzr\")\n+\n+# Environment variables that would let the caller's uv configuration\n+# redirect where packages come from or silently add requirements.  The\n+# Pipfile's ``[[source]]`` blocks and package specs are authoritative,\n+# so these are removed from the uv subprocess environment.\n+_SCRUBBED_UV_ENV = (\n+    \"UV_CONSTRAINT\",\n+    \"UV_DEFAULT_INDEX\",\n+    \"UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL\",\n+    \"UV_FIND_LINKS\",\n+    \"UV_INDEX\",\n+    \"UV_INDEX_STRATEGY\",\n+    \"UV_INDEX_URL\",\n+    \"UV_NO_INDEX\",\n+    \"UV_NO_SOURCES\",\n+    \"UV_NO_SOURCES_PACKAGE\",\n+    \"UV_OVERRIDE\",\n+    \"UV_PRERELEASE\",\n+    \"UV_TORCH_BACKEND\",\n+)\n+\n+INSTALL_HINT = (\n+    \"uv was not found on $PATH.  Install it with one of:\\n\"\n+    \"    pip install uv\\n\"\n+    \"    pipx install uv\\n\"\n+    \"    curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\\n\"\n+    \"See https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/\"\n+)\n+\n+\n+def find_uv() -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"Return the path to the ``uv`` executable, or ``None``.\"\"\"\n+    return shutil.which(\"uv\")\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class _Dependency:\n+    \"\"\"One top-level package from the request, prepared for uv.\"\"\"\n+\n+    name: str\n+    pep508: str\n+    extras: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n+    markers: str | None = None\n+    index: str | None = None\n+    index_url: str | None = None\n+    lock_index: str | None = None\n+    path: str | None = None\n+    abs_path: str | None = None\n+    file: str | None = None\n+    vcs: VCSPin | None = None\n+    editable: bool = False\n+    skip: bool = False\n+    specifier: str = \"\"\n+\n+\n+@dataclass\n+class _CompiledEntry:\n+    \"\"\"One requirement block parsed from ``uv pip compile`` output.\"\"\"\n+\n+    line: str\n+    hashes: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n+    via: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n+\n+\n+class UvBackend:\n+    \"\"\"Resolver backend that drives ``uv pip compile``.\"\"\"\n+\n+    name: str = \"uv\"\n+    install_hint: str = INSTALL_HINT\n+\n+    def is_available(self) -> bool:\n+        return find_uv() is not None\n+\n+    def resolve(self, request: ResolverRequest) -> ResolverResponse:\n+        \"\"\"Resolve ``request`` with uv.  Never raises; failures are\n+        returned as structured ``ResolutionError`` / ``InternalError``.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        started = time.monotonic()\n+        uv = find_uv()\n+        if uv is None:\n+            return _internal_error(INSTALL_HINT)\n+        try:\n+            with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"pipenv-uv-\") as workdir:\n+                return self._resolve_in(request, uv, Path(workdir), started)\n+        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:\n+            return _internal_error(\n+                f\"uv did not finish resolving within {exc.timeout:.0f} seconds.\"\n+            )\n+        except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 \u2014 backend contract: never raise\n+            return _internal_error(str(exc), traceback.format_exc())\n+\n+    def _resolve_in(\n+        self, request: ResolverRequest, uv: str, workdir: Path, started: float\n+    ) -> ResolverResponse:\n+        sources = list(request.sources) or [_DEFAULT_SOURCE]\n+        url_to_name = {_normalize_url(s.url): s.name for s in sources}\n+        pipfile_entries, foreign_pins = _pipfile_context(request.category)\n+\n+        deps: list[_Dependency] = []\n+        for name, spec in request.packages.specs.items():\n+            dep = _parse_spec(name, spec, pipfile_entries.get(name), url_to_name)\n+            if dep.index_url and dep.index not in url_to_name.values():\n+                # ``-i URL`` naming an index that isn't a Pipfile source.\n+                sources.append(Source(name=dep.index or \"\", url=dep.index_url))\n+                url_to_name[_normalize_url(dep.index_url)] = dep.index or \"\"\n+            deps.append(dep)\n+\n+        warnings: list[str] = []\n+        if request.extra_pip_args:\n+            warnings.append(\n+                \"The uv resolver backend ignores extra pip arguments: \"\n+                + \" \".join(request.extra_pip_args)\n+            )\n+\n+        index_pins = {\n+            _canonical(name): index\n+            for name, index in foreign_pins.items()\n+        }\n+        for dep in deps:\n+            if dep.index:\n+                index_pins[_canonical(dep.name)] = dep.index\n+        # Like the pip backend, a pin naming an index that isn't a source\n+        # restricts nothing: the package resolves from the primary index.\n+        # Direct references (VCS, file, path) don't come from an index.\n+        known = set(url_to_name.values())\n+        direct = {\n+            _canonical(dep.name) for dep in deps if dep.vcs or dep.file or dep.path\n+        }\n+        index_pins = {\n+            k: v for k, v in index_pins.items() if v in known and k not in direct\n+        }\n+        # A pin only reaches a package uv is resolving as a requirement,\n+        # so foreign pins become requirements as well.  Resolving without\n+        # them first to see which are needed isn't an option: that pass\n+        # could fetch, and even build, a same-named package from the\n+        # primary index.\n+        top_level = {_canonical(dep.name) for dep in deps}\n+        pin_only = frozenset(\n+            k for k, v in index_pins.items()\n+            if k not in top_level and v != sources[0].name\n+        )\n+        pyproject = workdir / \"pyproject.toml\"\n+        pyproject.write_text(\n+            _render_pyproject(deps, sources, index_pins, pin_only), encoding=\"utf-8\"\n+        )\n+\n+        cmd = [\n+            uv,\n+            \"pip\",\n+            \"compile\",\n+            str(pyproject),\n+            \"--no-config\",\n+            \"--python\",\n+            sys.executable,\n+            \"--generate-hashes\",\n+            \"--no-header\",\n+            \"--color\",\n+            \"never\",\n+            \"--no-progress\",\n+            \"--prerelease\",\n+            \"allow\" if request.options.pre else \"explicit\",\n+        ]\n+        if request.python_marker_override:\n+            cmd += [\"--python-version\", request.python_marker_override]\n+        if request.options.clear:\n+            cmd.append(\"--refresh\")\n+        if request.options.verbose:\n+            cmd.append(\"--verbose\")\n+        for source in sources:\n+            if not source.verify_ssl:\n+                host = urlsplit(source.url).netloc.rpartition(\"@\")[2]\n+                if host:\n+                    cmd += [\"--allow-insecure-host\", host]\n+        constraints = _render_constraints(request)\n+        if constraints:\n+            constraints_file = workdir / \"constraints.txt\"\n+            constraints_file.write_text(constraints, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+            cmd += [\"--constraint\", str(constraints_file)]\n+\n+        proc = subprocess.run(\n+            cmd,\n+            check=False,\n+            cwd=workdir,\n+            env=_uv_environment(sources[0].url),\n+            capture_output=True,\n+            text=True,\n+            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n+            errors=\"replace\",\n+            timeout=request.metadata.deadline_seconds,\n+        )\n+        log = [\" \".join(cmd)]\n+        if request.options.verbose:\n+            log.extend(proc.stderr.splitlines())\n+        diagnostics = Diagnostics(\n+            warnings=tuple(warnings),\n+            elapsed_seconds=time.monotonic() - started,\n+            resolver_log=tuple(log),\n+        )\n+        for warning in warnings:\n+            print(warning, file=sys.stderr)\n+\n+        if proc.returncode == 1:\n+            # uv exits 1 for unsatisfiable requirements and for packages\n+            # that can't be found \u2014 both user-actionable.\n+            return ResolverResponse(\n+                schema_version=SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+                result=ResolutionError(\n+                    kind=\"resolution_error\",\n+                    conflicts=(),\n+                    pip_message=proc.stderr.strip(),\n+                ),\n+                diagnostics=diagnostics,\n+            )\n+        if proc.returncode != 0:\n+            return _internal_error(\n+                f\"uv pip compile exited with status {proc.returncode}:\\n\"\n+                f\"{proc.stderr.strip()}\",\n+                diagnostics=diagnostics,\n+            )\n+\n+        locked = _translate(\n+            _parse_compile_output(proc.stdout),\n+            deps,\n+            index_pins,\n+            pin_only,\n+        )\n+        return ResolverResponse(\n+            schema_version=SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+            result=ResolverSuccess(kind=\"success\", locked=locked),\n+            diagnostics=diagnostics,\n+        )\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Request \u2192 uv input\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _parse_spec(\n+    name: str,\n+    spec: str,\n+    pipfile_entry: Any,\n+    url_to_name: Mapping[str, str],\n+) -> _Dependency:\n+    \"\"\"Translate one wire-shape spec (a pip-install argument line, as\n+    produced by ``convert_deps_to_pip``) into a :class:`_Dependency`.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    from pipenv.utils.dependencies import translate_markers\n+    from pipenv.utils.indexes import parse_indexes\n+    from pipenv.vendor.packaging.markers import Marker\n+    from pipenv.vendor.packaging.requirements import Requirement\n+\n+    entry = pipfile_entry if isinstance(pipfile_entry, dict) else {}\n+    index_url, _extra, _trusted, remainder = parse_indexes(spec)\n+    editable = bool(entry.get(\"editable\"))\n+    if remainder and remainder[0] in (\"-e\", \"--editable\"):\n+        editable = True\n+        remainder = remainder[1:]\n+    text = \" \".join(remainder).strip()\n+    if _is_legacy_vcs(text):\n+        # The install line always says ``-e`` for these, whatever the\n+        # Pipfile asks for, and leaves out the markers.\n+        if isinstance(pipfile_entry, dict):\n+            editable = bool(entry.get(\"editable\"))\n+        text = _legacy_vcs_to_pep508(\n+            name, text, translate_markers(entry).get(\"markers\")\n+        )\n+    elif \" @ \" in text:\n+        # The install line has ``URL; marker``, but PEP 508 requires\n+        # whitespace after a URL.\n+        text = text.replace(\"; \", \" ; \", 1)\n+\n+    index = entry.get(\"index\")\n+    if index_url and not index:\n+        index = url_to_name.get(_normalize_url(index_url))\n+        if index is None:\n+            index = f\"pipenv-index-{len(url_to_name)}\"\n+    # The lockfile ``index`` field follows the pip backend's rule: a\n+    # dict-style Pipfile entry records only an explicit ``index``; a\n+    # plain string entry records the index it resolves from.\n+    if isinstance(pipfile_entry, dict):\n+        lock_index = entry.get(\"index\")\n+    else:\n+        lock_index = index or (next(iter(url_to_name.values()), None))\n+    dep = _Dependency(\n+        name=name,\n+        pep508=\"\",\n+        editable=editable,\n+        index=index,\n+        index_url=index_url,\n+        lock_index=lock_index,\n+        skip=bool(entry.get(\"skip_resolver\")),\n+    )\n+\n+    if \" @ \" not in text and (\n+        entry.get(\"path\") or entry.get(\"file\") or _looks_like_path(text)\n+    ):\n+        # ``location[extras]; marker``\n+        requirement, _, marker = text.partition(\"; \")\n+        extras = re.search(r\"\\[([^\\]]*)\\]$\", requirement)\n+        if extras:\n+            requirement = requirement[: extras.start()]\n+            dep.extras = tuple(\n+                sorted(e.strip() for e in extras.group(1).split(\",\") if e.strip())\n+            )\n+        if marker:\n+            dep.markers = str(Marker(marker)).replace('\"', \"'\")\n+        location = entry.get(\"path\") or entry.get(\"file\") or requirement\n+        dep.abs_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(requirement))\n+        if entry.get(\"file\"):\n+            dep.file = location\n+        else:\n+            dep.path = location\n+        dep.pep508 = name\n+        if dep.file and not editable:\n+            # Refer to the file directly: a bare ``name`` with no path\n+            # source would make uv look it up on the index.\n+            extra_text = f\"[{','.join(dep.extras)}]\" if dep.extras else \"\"\n+            marker_text = f\" ; {dep.markers}\" if dep.markers else \"\"\n+            uri = Path(dep.abs_path).as_uri()\n+            dep.pep508 = f\"{name}{extra_text} @ {uri}{marker_text}\"\n+        dep.index = dep.lock_index = None\n+        return dep\n+\n+    req = Requirement(text)\n+    dep.extras = tuple(sorted(req.extras))\n+    if req.marker is not None:\n+        dep.markers = str(req.marker).replace('\"', \"'\")\n+    dep.specifier = str(req.specifier)\n+    if req.url:\n+        dep.index = dep.lock_index = None\n+        scheme = req.url.split(\"+\", 1)[0] if \"+\" in req.url.split(\":\", 1)[0] else \"\"\n+        if scheme in _VCS_SCHEMES:\n+            dep.vcs = _vcs_pin(req.url)\n+        elif req.url.startswith(\"file:\"):\n+            dep.abs_path = _file_url_to_path(req.url)\n+            dep.file = entry.get(\"file\") or entry.get(\"path\") or req.url\n+        else:\n+            dep.file = req.url\n+    dep.pep508 = str(req)\n+    return dep\n+\n+\n+def _render_pyproject(\n+    deps: Sequence[_Dependency],\n+    sources: Sequence[Source],\n+    index_pins: Mapping[str, str],\n+    pin_only: frozenset[str] = frozenset(),\n+) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Render the throwaway ``pyproject.toml`` uv compiles.\n+\n+    JSON string literals are valid TOML basic strings, so ``json.dumps``\n+    does the quoting.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    q = json.dumps\n+    lines = [\n+        \"[project]\",\n+        f\"name = {q(_ROOT_PROJECT)}\",\n+        'version = \"0\"',\n+        \"dependencies = [\",\n+    ]\n+    for dep in deps:\n+        if dep.skip:\n+            continue\n+        if dep.abs_path and dep.vcs is None and (dep.path or dep.editable):\n+            requirement = dep.name + (f\"[{','.join(dep.extras)}]\" if dep.extras else \"\")\n+            if dep.markers:\n+                requirement += f\" ; {dep.markers}\"\n+        else:\n+            requirement = dep.pep508\n+        lines.append(f\"    {q(requirement)},\")\n+    lines.extend(f\"    {q(name)},\" for name in sorted(pin_only))\n+    lines.append(\"]\")\n+    lines.append(\"\")\n+    lines.append(\"[tool.uv.sources]\")\n+    for dep in deps:\n+        if dep.skip or not dep.abs_path or dep.vcs is not None:\n+            continue\n+        if dep.path or dep.editable:\n+            editable = \"true\" if dep.editable else \"false\"\n+            lines.append(\n+                f\"{q(_canonical(dep.name))} = \"\n+                f\"{{ path = {q(dep.abs_path)}, editable = {editable} }}\"\n+            )\n+    primary = sources[0].name\n+    for name, index in sorted(index_pins.items()):\n+        if index != primary:\n+            lines.append(f\"{q(name)} = {{ index = {q(_uv_index_name(index))} }}\")\n+    # The primary index is uv's default index (see ``_uv_environment``).\n+    for source in sources[1:]:\n+        lines.append(\"\")\n+        lines.append(\"[[tool.uv.index]]\")\n+        lines.append(f\"name = {q(_uv_index_name(source.name))}\")\n+        lines.append(f\"url = {q(source.url)}\")\n+        lines.append(\"explicit = true\")\n+    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def _render_constraints(request: ResolverRequest) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Pin the already-resolved default-category packages so that\n+    non-default categories resolve consistently with them.\"\"\"\n+    resolved = request.resolved_default_deps\n+    if resolved is None:\n+        return \"\"\n+    lines = []\n+    for entry in resolved.entries:\n+        if entry.vcs is not None:\n+            ref = f\"@{entry.vcs.ref}\" if entry.vcs.ref else \"\"\n+            subdirectory = (\n+                f\"#subdirectory={entry.vcs.subdirectory}\"\n+                if entry.vcs.subdirectory\n+                else \"\"\n+            )\n+            lines.append(\n+                f\"{entry.name} @ {entry.vcs.backend}+{entry.vcs.url}{ref}{subdirectory}\"\n+            )\n+        elif entry.version and entry.version.startswith(\"==\"):\n+            lines.append(f\"{entry.name}{entry.version}\")\n+    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + (\"\\n\" if lines else \"\")\n+\n+\n+def _uv_environment(default_index: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n+    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in _SCRUBBED_UV_ENV}\n+    env[\"UV_DEFAULT_INDEX\"] = default_index\n+    # Pipenv forwards its keyring setting to pip as PIP_KEYRING_PROVIDER\n+    # (gh-5715); uv reads its own variable and only knows ``disabled``\n+    # and ``subprocess``, so pip's ``auto`` / ``import`` map to the\n+    # latter.\n+    keyring = env.get(\"PIP_KEYRING_PROVIDER\")\n+    if keyring and \"UV_KEYRING_PROVIDER\" not in env:\n+        env[\"UV_KEYRING_PROVIDER\"] = \"disabled\" if keyring == \"disabled\" else \"subprocess\"\n+    env.setdefault(\"UV_NO_PROGRESS\", \"1\")\n+    return env\n+\n+\n+def _pipfile_context(category: str) -> tuple[dict, dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Best-effort read of the project's Pipfile, mirroring what the pip\n+    backend's ``Resolver.create`` reads inside the resolver subprocess.\n+\n+    Returns ``(entries, foreign_pins)``: the Pipfile entries of\n+    ``category`` (for ``editable`` / ``file`` / ``path`` /\n+    ``skip_resolver`` details the wire spec doesn't carry), and, for\n+    non-default categories, the ``index`` pins declared in *other*\n+    categories so their transitive use resolves from the right index.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        from pipenv.project import Project\n+\n+        project = Project(chdir=False)\n+        if not project.pipfile.exists:\n+            return {}, {}\n+        pipfile = project.pipfile\n+        entries = dict(pipfile.get_section(category) or {})\n+        foreign: dict[str, str] = {}\n+        if category and category != \"packages\":\n+            for other in pipfile.get_package_categories():\n+                if other == category:\n+                    continue\n+                for name, entry in (pipfile.get_section(other) or {}).items():\n+                    if isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get(\"index\"):\n+                        foreign.setdefault(name, entry[\"index\"])\n+        return entries, foreign\n+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 \u2014 no project on disk \u2192 spec-only\n+        return {}, {}\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# uv output \u2192 LockedRequirement\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _parse_compile_output(text: str) -> list[_CompiledEntry]:\n+    \"\"\"Parse ``uv pip compile`` requirements-format output.\n+\n+    Each requirement starts on an unindented line; ``--hash`` lines and\n+    ``# via`` annotations follow, indented.  ``# via`` is\n+    either inline (single parent) or followed by ``#   parent`` lines.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    entries: list[_CompiledEntry] = []\n+    current: _CompiledEntry | None = None\n+    in_via = False\n+    for raw in text.splitlines():\n+        stripped = raw.strip()\n+        if not stripped:\n+            continue\n+        if not raw[0].isspace() and not stripped.startswith(\"#\"):\n+            tokens = stripped.rstrip(\"\\\\\").split(\" --hash=\")\n+            current = _CompiledEntry(line=tokens[0].strip())\n+            current.hashes.extend(t.strip() for t in tokens[1:])\n+            entries.append(current)\n+            in_via = False\n+            continue\n+        if current is None:\n+            continue\n+        if stripped.startswith(\"--hash=\"):\n+            current.hashes.append(stripped[len(\"--hash=\") :].rstrip(\"\\\\\").strip())\n+            in_via = False\n+        elif stripped.startswith(\"# via\"):\n+            rest = stripped[len(\"# via\") :].strip()\n+            in_via = not rest\n+            if rest:\n+                current.via.append(rest)\n+        elif in_via and stripped.startswith(\"#\"):\n+            current.via.append(stripped.lstrip(\"#\").strip())\n+    return entries\n+\n+\n+def _translate(\n+    entries: Sequence[_CompiledEntry],\n+    deps: Sequence[_Dependency],\n+    index_pins: Mapping[str, str],\n+    pin_only: frozenset[str] = frozenset(),\n+) -> tuple[LockedRequirement, ...]:\n+    from pipenv.utils.dependencies import pep423_name\n+    from pipenv.vendor.packaging.requirements import Requirement\n+\n+    top_level = {_canonical(dep.name): dep for dep in deps}\n+    by_path = {\n+        os.path.normcase(dep.abs_path): dep for dep in deps if dep.abs_path\n+    }\n+\n+    resolved: dict[str, tuple[_CompiledEntry, _Dependency | None, Any]] = {}\n+    for entry in entries:\n+        dep: _Dependency | None = None\n+        req = None\n+        # uv prints local path requirements without a name: ``-e /path``\n+        # when editable, otherwise just ``/path``.\n+        location = None\n+        if entry.line.startswith((\"-e \", \"--editable \")):\n+            location = entry.line.split(None, 1)[1].strip()\n+        elif entry.line.startswith(\"file:\") or _looks_like_path(entry.line):\n+            location = entry.line\n+        if location is not None:\n+            if location.startswith(\"file:\"):\n+                location = _file_url_to_path(location)\n+            dep = by_path.get(os.path.normcase(os.path.abspath(location)))\n+            if dep is None:\n+                continue\n+            key = _canonical(dep.name)\n+        else:\n+            req = Requirement(entry.line)\n+            key = _canonical(req.name)\n+            dep = top_level.get(key)\n+        resolved[key] = (entry, dep, req)\n+\n+    parents: dict[str, set[str]] = {}\n+    for key, (entry, _dep, _req) in resolved.items():\n+        parents[key] = set()\n+        for via in entry.via:\n+            if via.startswith(_ROOT_PROJECT):\n+                parents[key].add(\"\")\n+            elif not via.startswith(\"-\"):\n+                parents[key].add(_canonical(via.split()[0]))\n+    if pin_only:\n+        for key in _unneeded_pin_only(parents, pin_only):\n+            del resolved[key]\n+            del parents[key]\n+    markers = _fold_markers(parents, top_level)\n+\n+    locked: list[LockedRequirement] = []\n+    for key, (entry, dep, req) in resolved.items():\n+        name = pep423_name(dep.name if dep else req.name)\n+        index = dep.lock_index if dep is not None else index_pins.get(key)\n+        fields: dict[str, Any] = {\n+            \"name\": name,\n+            \"extras\": dep.extras if dep else (),\n+            \"markers\": markers.get(key),\n+            \"hashes\": tuple(sorted(set(entry.hashes))),\n+            \"index\": index,\n+            \"editable\": bool(dep and dep.editable),\n+        }\n+        if dep is not None and (dep.path or dep.file) and dep.vcs is None:\n+            fields[\"path\"] = dep.path\n+            fields[\"file\"] = dep.file\n+        elif dep is not None and dep.vcs is not None:\n+            pinned_vcs = _vcs_pin(req.url) if req is not None and req.url else dep.vcs\n+            fields[\"vcs\"] = VCSPin(\n+                backend=pinned_vcs.backend,\n+                url=pinned_vcs.url,\n+                ref=pinned_vcs.ref or dep.vcs.ref,\n+                subdirectory=pinned_vcs.subdirectory or dep.vcs.subdirectory,\n+            )\n+        elif req is not None and req.url:\n+            fields[\"file\"] = req.url\n+        else:\n+            fields[\"version\"] = \"==\" + next(iter(req.specifier)).version\n+        locked.append(LockedRequirement(**fields))\n+\n+    # Top-level packages uv left out because their markers don't apply\n+    # to this environment.  The pip backend records them anyway (from\n+    # the Pipfile entry, without hashes) so the lockfile still installs\n+    # them on the platforms they target; do the same.\n+    for key, dep in top_level.items():\n+        if key in resolved or not (dep.markers or dep.skip):\n+            continue\n+        locked.append(\n+            LockedRequirement(\n+                name=pep423_name(dep.name),\n+                version=None if (dep.vcs or dep.path or dep.file) else (dep.specifier or \"*\"),\n+                extras=dep.extras,\n+                markers=dep.markers,\n+                index=dep.lock_index,\n+                vcs=dep.vcs,\n+                path=dep.path,\n+                file=dep.file,\n+                editable=dep.editable,\n+            )\n+        )\n+    return tuple(locked)\n+\n+\n+def _fold_markers(\n+    parents: Mapping[str, set[str]], top_level: Mapping[str, _Dependency]\n+) -> dict[str, str | None]:\n+    \"\"\"Compute each package's marker from the markers of the top-level\n+    packages that pull it in.\n+\n+    A package needed by any unconditional path gets no marker; one\n+    reached only through marker-guarded top-level packages gets the OR\n+    of their markers.  ``\"\"`` in ``parents`` means \"required directly\n+    by the project\".\n+    \"\"\"\n+    folded: dict[str, str | None] = {}\n+    for key in parents:\n+        seen = {key}\n+        stack = [key]\n+        found: set[str] = set()\n+        unconditional = False\n+        while stack and not unconditional:\n+            current = stack.pop()\n+            for parent in parents.get(current, ()):\n+                if parent == \"\":\n+                    dep = top_level.get(current)\n+                    if dep is None or not dep.markers:\n+                        unconditional = True\n+                        break\n+                    found.add(dep.markers)\n+                elif parent not in seen:\n+                    seen.add(parent)\n+                    stack.append(parent)\n+        if unconditional or not found:\n+            # ``not found``: only reachable through an unknown parent\n+            # (e.g. a constraints file).\n+            folded[key] = None\n+        elif len(found) == 1:\n+            folded[key] = next(iter(found))\n+        else:\n+            folded[key] = \" or \".join(f\"({m})\" for m in sorted(found))\n+    return folded\n+\n+\n+def _unneeded_pin_only(\n+    parents: dict[str, set[str]], pin_only: frozenset[str]\n+) -> set[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Return the packages only in the result because of a ``pin_only``\n+    requirement, and remove those requirements' edges from ``parents``.\"\"\"\n+    roots = [\n+        key\n+        for key, ups in parents.items()\n+        if key not in pin_only and (\"\" in ups or not ups)\n+    ]\n+    for key in pin_only:\n+        parents.get(key, set()).discard(\"\")\n+    children: dict[str, set[str]] = {}\n+    for key, ups in parents.items():\n+        for parent in ups:\n+            children.setdefault(parent, set()).add(key)\n+    needed = set(roots)\n+    stack = list(roots)\n+    while stack:\n+        for child in children.get(stack.pop(), ()):\n+            if child not in needed:\n+                needed.add(child)\n+                stack.append(child)\n+    return set(parents) - needed\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Helpers\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _internal_error(\n+    message: str, tb: str | None = None, diagnostics: Diagnostics | None = None\n+) -> ResolverResponse:\n+    return ResolverResponse(\n+        schema_version=SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+        result=InternalError(kind=\"internal_error\", message=message, traceback=tb),\n+        diagnostics=diagnostics or Diagnostics(),\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def _canonical(name: str) -> str:\n+    from pipenv.vendor.packaging.utils import canonicalize_name\n+\n+    return canonicalize_name(name)\n+\n+\n+def _uv_index_name(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"uv index names allow only ASCII alphanumerics, ``-``, ``_``, ``.``.\"\"\"\n+    return \"\".join(c if c.isascii() and (c.isalnum() or c in \"-_.\") else \"-\" for c in name)\n+\n+\n+def _normalize_url(url: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Strip credentials and trailing slashes so an ``-i URL`` in a spec\n+    matches the Pipfile source it names.\"\"\"\n+    parts = urlsplit(url.strip())\n+    netloc = parts.netloc.rpartition(\"@\")[2].lower()\n+    return urlunsplit((parts.scheme.lower(), netloc, parts.path.rstrip(\"/\"), \"\", \"\"))\n+\n+\n+def _looks_like_path(text: str) -> bool:\n+    if not text or \" @ \" in text:\n+        return False\n+    return (\n+        text.startswith((\".\", \"/\", \"~\", \"\\\\\"))\n+        or (len(text) > 1 and text[1] == \":\")  # Windows drive\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def _is_legacy_vcs(text: str) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Whether ``text`` is a bare ``git+URL`` rather than a PEP 508 line.\"\"\"\n+    scheme, plus, _ = text.partition(\"+\")\n+    return bool(plus) and scheme in _VCS_SCHEMES and \" @ \" not in text\n+\n+\n+def _legacy_vcs_to_pep508(name: str, text: str, markers: str | None) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Turn ``git+file:///repo@ref#egg=pkg&subdirectory=sub[extra]``, the\n+    form ``dependency_as_pip_install_line`` emits for local repositories,\n+    into ``pkg[extra] @ git+file:///repo@ref#subdirectory=sub``.\"\"\"\n+    extras = \"\"\n+    match = re.search(r\"\\[[^\\]]*\\]$\", text)\n+    if match:\n+        extras = match.group()\n+        text = text[: match.start()]\n+    url, _, fragment = text.partition(\"#\")\n+    kept = [i for i in fragment.split(\"&\") if i and not i.startswith(\"egg=\")]\n+    backend, _, location = url.partition(\"+\")\n+    if \"://\" not in location:\n+        # A local repository given as a path.\n+        path, at, ref = location.rpartition(\"@\")\n+        if not at:\n+            path, ref = location, \"\"\n+        absolute = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(path))\n+        location = Path(absolute).as_uri() + (f\"@{ref}\" if ref else \"\")\n+    pep508 = f\"{name}{extras} @ {backend}+{location}\"\n+    if kept:\n+        pep508 += \"#\" + \"&\".join(kept)\n+    if markers:\n+        pep508 += f\" ; {markers}\"\n+    return pep508\n+\n+\n+def _file_url_to_path(url: str) -> str:\n+    parts = urlsplit(url)\n+    path = unquote(parts.path)\n+    if os.name == \"nt\" and path.startswith(\"/\") and len(path) > 2 and path[2] == \":\":\n+        path = path[1:]\n+    return os.path.abspath(path)\n+\n+\n+def _vcs_pin(url: str) -> VCSPin:\n+    \"\"\"Split ``git+https://host/repo.git@ref#subdirectory=x`` into a\n+    :class:`VCSPin`.\"\"\"\n+    backend, _, rest = url.partition(\"+\")\n+    parts = urlsplit(rest)\n+    path, sep, ref = parts.path.rpartition(\"@\")\n+    if not sep:\n+        path, ref = parts.path, \"\"\n+    subdirectory = None\n+    for item in parts.fragment.split(\"&\"):\n+        key, _, value = item.partition(\"=\")\n+        if key == \"subdirectory\" and value:\n+            subdirectory = value\n+    return VCSPin(\n+        backend=backend,\n+        url=urlunsplit((parts.scheme, parts.netloc, path, parts.query, \"\")),\n+        ref=ref or None,\n+        subdirectory=subdirectory,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+__all__ = [\"UvBackend\", \"find_uv\", \"INSTALL_HINT\"]\ndiff --git a/pipenv/resolver/core.py b/pipenv/resolver/core.py\nindex a9f3f31405..8d3431a248 100644\n--- a/pipenv/resolver/core.py\n+++ b/pipenv/resolver/core.py\n@@ -729,13 +729,17 @@ def resolve_for_pipenv(request: ResolverRequest) -> ResolverResponse:\n         )\n \n     if not backend.is_available():\n+        # Backends that depend on an external tool (e.g. uv) carry an\n+        # ``install_hint`` naming the binary and how to install it.\n+        install_hint = getattr(backend, \"install_hint\", None)\n+        hint = f\"\\n{install_hint}\\n\" if install_hint else \"  \"\n         return ResolverResponse(\n             schema_version=SCHEMA_VERSION,\n             result=InternalError(\n                 kind=\"internal_error\",\n                 message=(\n                     f\"Resolver backend {backend_name!r} is not available \"\n-                    f\"on this machine.  Install it and re-run, or remove \"\n+                    f\"on this machine.{hint}Install it and re-run, or remove \"\n                     f\"the [pipenv] resolver setting from your Pipfile / \"\n                     f\"unset PIPENV_RESOLVER / pass --resolver pip.\"\n                 ),\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/integration/test_lock_uv_backend.py b/tests/integration/test_lock_uv_backend.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..caa253d44b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/tests/integration/test_lock_uv_backend.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,248 @@\n+\"\"\"Integration tests for the ``uv`` resolver backend (gh-6109).\n+\n+Skipped unless a ``uv`` binary is on ``$PATH``.  Both tests use the\n+offline ``file://`` index fixture or indexes they generate, so they need\n+no network access.\n+\"\"\"\n+import hashlib\n+import shutil\n+import subprocess\n+import zipfile\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+pytestmark = [\n+    pytest.mark.lock,\n+    pytest.mark.skipif(shutil.which(\"uv\") is None, reason=\"uv is not installed\"),\n+]\n+\n+\n+def _strip_requires_python_markers(section):\n+    \"\"\"The pip backend AND-merges each package's Requires-Python into\n+    ``markers``; uv doesn't report Requires-Python.  Drop markers that\n+    consist only of ``python_version`` clauses before comparing.\"\"\"\n+    cleaned = {}\n+    for name, entry in section.items():\n+        entry = dict(entry)\n+        markers = entry.get(\"markers\", \"\")\n+        if markers and all(\n+            clause.strip().startswith(\"python_version\")\n+            for clause in markers.split(\" and \")\n+        ):\n+            del entry[\"markers\"]\n+        cleaned[name] = entry\n+    return cleaned\n+\n+\n+def _write_wheel(directory, name, version, requires=()):\n+    \"\"\"Write a minimal wheel into ``directory`` and return its path.\"\"\"\n+    directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n+    wheel = directory / f\"{name}-{version}-py3-none-any.whl\"\n+    dist_info = f\"{name}-{version}.dist-info\"\n+    metadata = f\"Metadata-Version: 2.1\\nName: {name}\\nVersion: {version}\\n\"\n+    metadata += \"\".join(f\"Requires-Dist: {r}\\n\" for r in requires)\n+    with zipfile.ZipFile(wheel, \"w\") as archive:\n+        archive.writestr(f\"{name}.py\", \"\")\n+        archive.writestr(f\"{dist_info}/METADATA\", metadata)\n+        archive.writestr(\n+            f\"{dist_info}/WHEEL\",\n+            \"Wheel-Version: 1.0\\nGenerator: test\\nRoot-Is-Purelib: true\\n\"\n+            \"Tag: py3-none-any\\n\",\n+        )\n+        archive.writestr(f\"{dist_info}/RECORD\", \"\")\n+    return wheel\n+\n+\n+def _add_to_index(root, name, version, requires=()):\n+    \"\"\"Add a package to the simple index at ``root``; return the wheel.\"\"\"\n+    wheel = _write_wheel(root / name, name, version, requires)\n+    links = \"\".join(\n+        f'<a href=\"{w.name}\">{w.name}</a>' for w in sorted((root / name).glob(\"*.whl\"))\n+    )\n+    (root / name / \"index.html\").write_text(f\"<html><body>{links}</body></html>\")\n+    return wheel\n+\n+\n+def _write_two_index_pipfile(p, public, private, packages, dev_packages):\n+    Path(p.pipfile_path).write_text(\n+        f\"\"\"\n+[[source]]\n+url = \"{public.as_uri()}/\"\n+verify_ssl = true\n+name = \"public\"\n+\n+[[source]]\n+url = \"{private.as_uri()}/\"\n+verify_ssl = true\n+name = \"private\"\n+\n+[packages]\n+{packages}\n+\n+[dev-packages]\n+{dev_packages}\n+\"\"\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def test_uv_backend_pin_in_other_category_restricts_transitive_use(\n+    pipenv_instance_file_pypi, tmp_path\n+):\n+    public, private = tmp_path / \"public\", tmp_path / \"private\"\n+    _add_to_index(public, \"shared\", \"2.0\")\n+    _add_to_index(public, \"devtool\", \"1.0\", requires=[\"shared\"])\n+    wheel = _add_to_index(private, \"shared\", \"1.0\")\n+    with pipenv_instance_file_pypi() as p:\n+        _write_two_index_pipfile(\n+            p,\n+            public,\n+            private,\n+            'shared = {version = \"*\", index = \"private\"}',\n+            'devtool = \"*\"',\n+        )\n+        c = p.pipenv(\"lock --backend uv\")\n+        assert c.returncode == 0, c.stderr\n+        expected = f\"sha256:{hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\"\n+        for section in (\"default\", \"develop\"):\n+            entry = p.lockfile[section][\"shared\"]\n+            assert entry[\"version\"] == \"==1.0\"\n+            assert entry[\"hashes\"] == [expected]\n+            assert entry[\"index\"] == \"private\"\n+\n+\n+def test_uv_backend_unused_pin_in_other_category_is_not_locked(\n+    pipenv_instance_file_pypi, tmp_path\n+):\n+    public, private = tmp_path / \"public\", tmp_path / \"private\"\n+    _add_to_index(public, \"devtool\", \"1.0\")\n+    _add_to_index(private, \"helper\", \"1.0\")\n+    _add_to_index(private, \"shared\", \"1.0\", requires=[\"helper\"])\n+    _add_to_index(public, \"helper\", \"1.0\")\n+    with pipenv_instance_file_pypi() as p:\n+        _write_two_index_pipfile(\n+            p,\n+            public,\n+            private,\n+            'shared = {version = \"*\", index = \"private\"}',\n+            'devtool = \"*\"',\n+        )\n+        c = p.pipenv(\"lock --backend uv\")\n+        assert c.returncode == 0, c.stderr\n+        assert set(p.lockfile[\"develop\"]) == {\"devtool\"}\n+\n+\n+def test_uv_backend_local_requirements(pipenv_instance_file_pypi, tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"Each local form the Pipfile can express, through a real uv run.\"\"\"\n+    index = tmp_path / \"index\"\n+    _add_to_index(index, \"helper\", \"1.0\")\n+    wheel = _write_wheel(tmp_path / \"wheels\", \"localwheel\", \"1.0\")\n+\n+    def write_project(root, name):\n+        root.mkdir(parents=True)\n+        (root / f\"{name}.py\").write_text(\"\")\n+        (root / \"pyproject.toml\").write_text(\n+            f\"\"\"\n+[project]\n+name = \"{name}\"\n+version = \"1.0\"\n+[project.optional-dependencies]\n+test = [\"helper\"]\n+[build-system]\n+requires = [\"uv_build\"]\n+build-backend = \"uv_build\"\n+\"\"\"\n+        )\n+\n+    write_project(tmp_path / \"editablepkg\", \"editablepkg\")\n+    write_project(tmp_path / \"plainpkg\", \"plainpkg\")\n+    repo = tmp_path / \"repo\"\n+    write_project(repo / \"sub\", \"gitpkg\")\n+    git = [\"git\", \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@example.com\"]\n+    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", str(repo)], check=True)\n+    subprocess.run(git + [\"-C\", str(repo), \"add\", \".\"], check=True)\n+    subprocess.run(git + [\"-C\", str(repo), \"commit\", \"-qm\", \"init\"], check=True)\n+\n+    with pipenv_instance_file_pypi() as p:\n+        Path(p.pipfile_path).write_text(\n+            f\"\"\"\n+[[source]]\n+url = \"{index.as_uri()}/\"\n+verify_ssl = true\n+name = \"index\"\n+\n+[packages]\n+editablepkg = {{path = \"{tmp_path / 'editablepkg'}\", editable = true, extras = [\"test\"], markers = \"os_name != 'nonexistent'\"}}\n+plainpkg = {{path = \"{tmp_path / 'plainpkg'}\", extras = [\"test\"]}}\n+localwheel = {{file = \"{wheel}\"}}\n+gitpkg = {{git = \"{repo.as_uri()}\", subdirectory = \"sub\", extras = [\"test\"], markers = \"os_name != 'nonexistent'\"}}\n+\"\"\"\n+        )\n+        c = p.pipenv(\"lock --backend uv\")\n+        assert c.returncode == 0, c.stderr\n+        default = p.lockfile[\"default\"]\n+\n+    assert default[\"editablepkg\"][\"editable\"] is True\n+    assert default[\"editablepkg\"][\"extras\"] == [\"test\"]\n+    assert default[\"editablepkg\"][\"markers\"] == \"os_name != 'nonexistent'\"\n+    assert default[\"plainpkg\"][\"path\"] == str(tmp_path / \"plainpkg\")\n+    assert default[\"plainpkg\"][\"extras\"] == [\"test\"]\n+    assert default[\"localwheel\"][\"file\"] == str(wheel)\n+    expected = f\"sha256:{hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\"\n+    assert default[\"localwheel\"][\"hashes\"] == [expected]\n+    assert default[\"gitpkg\"][\"git\"] == repo.as_uri()\n+    assert default[\"gitpkg\"][\"subdirectory\"] == \"sub\"\n+    assert default[\"gitpkg\"][\"markers\"] == \"os_name != 'nonexistent'\"\n+    assert \"helper\" in default\n+\n+\n+def test_uv_backend_matches_pip_backend(pipenv_instance_file_pypi):\n+    with pipenv_instance_file_pypi() as p:\n+        with open(p.pipfile_path, \"w\") as f:\n+            f.write(\n+                f\"\"\"\n+[[source]]\n+url = \"{p.index_url}\"\n+verify_ssl = true\n+name = \"testindex\"\n+\n+[packages]\n+requests = \"==2.19.1\"\n+colorama = {{version = \"*\", markers = \"sys_platform == 'win32'\"}}\n+\n+[dev-packages]\n+six = \"*\"\n+\"\"\"\n+            )\n+        c = p.pipenv(\"lock --backend pip\")\n+        assert c.returncode == 0, c.stderr\n+        pip_lock = p.lockfile\n+\n+        c = p.pipenv(\"lock --backend uv\")\n+        assert c.returncode == 0, c.stderr\n+        uv_lock = p.lockfile\n+\n+        for section in (\"default\", \"develop\"):\n+            assert _strip_requires_python_markers(\n+                uv_lock[section]\n+            ) == _strip_requires_python_markers(pip_lock[section])\n+\n+\n+def test_uv_backend_reports_conflicts(pipenv_instance_file_pypi):\n+    with pipenv_instance_file_pypi() as p:\n+        with open(p.pipfile_path, \"w\") as f:\n+            f.write(\n+                f\"\"\"\n+[[source]]\n+url = \"{p.index_url}\"\n+verify_ssl = true\n+name = \"testindex\"\n+\n+[packages]\n+requests = \"==2.19.1\"\n+urllib3 = \"==1.20\"\n+\"\"\"\n+            )\n+        c = p.pipenv(\"lock --backend uv\")\n+        assert c.returncode != 0\n+        assert \"No solution found\" in c.stderr\ndiff --git a/tests/unit/test_resolver_backends.py b/tests/unit/test_resolver_backends.py\nindex d6a3101532..8b6e397e2d 100644\n--- a/tests/unit/test_resolver_backends.py\n+++ b/tests/unit/test_resolver_backends.py\n@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@ def test_backend_flag_rejects_unknown_choice(self, capsys):\n         import pytest\n \n         with pytest.raises(SystemExit):\n-            self._parse_lock_args([\"--backend\", \"uv\"])  # not in choices\n+            self._parse_lock_args([\"--backend\", \"poetry\"])  # not in choices\n         err_text = capsys.readouterr().err\n         assert \"invalid choice\" in err_text or \"argument\" in err_text\n \ndiff --git a/tests/unit/test_uv_backend.py b/tests/unit/test_uv_backend.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..f2feade1dc\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/tests/unit/test_uv_backend.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,641 @@\n+\"\"\"Unit tests for :class:`UvBackend` (gh-6109).\n+\n+The backend shells out to ``uv pip compile``; every test here mocks the\n+subprocess (and the Pipfile read) so no ``uv`` binary or network is\n+needed.  Coverage:\n+\n+* **Spec translation** \u2014 pip-install argument lines (extras, markers,\n+  ``-i`` index pins, VCS, file URLs, editable paths) become uv inputs.\n+* **Index restriction** \u2014 the generated ``pyproject.toml`` marks every\n+  non-primary source ``explicit = true`` so unpinned packages resolve\n+  only from the primary index.\n+* **Output parsing** \u2014 ``--hash`` and ``# via`` annotations, editable\n+  lines, and marker folding onto transitive dependencies.\n+* **Failure modes** \u2014 uv exit 1 \u2192 ``ResolutionError``; other non-zero\n+  exits \u2192 ``InternalError``; missing binary \u2192 ``InternalError`` with\n+  the install hint, both from the backend and from the dispatcher.\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from unittest import mock\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from pipenv.resolver.backends import get_backend, list_backends\n+from pipenv.resolver.backends import uv as uv_backend\n+from pipenv.resolver.backends.uv import (\n+    UvBackend,\n+    _fold_markers,\n+    _parse_compile_output,\n+    _parse_spec,\n+    _render_constraints,\n+    _render_pyproject,\n+    _unneeded_pin_only,\n+    _uv_environment,\n+    _vcs_pin,\n+)\n+from pipenv.resolver.schema import (\n+    SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+    InternalError,\n+    LockedRequirement,\n+    PackageSpecs,\n+    ResolutionError,\n+    ResolvedDeps,\n+    ResolverOptions,\n+    ResolverRequest,\n+    ResolverSuccess,\n+    Source,\n+    VCSPin,\n+)\n+\n+if sys.version_info >= (3, 11):\n+    import tomllib\n+else:  # pragma: no cover - exercised on 3.10 only\n+    tomllib = None\n+\n+_PYPI = \"https://pypi.org/simple\"\n+_PRIVATE = \"https://private.example.com/simple\"\n+_URL_TO_NAME = {_PYPI: \"pypi\", _PRIVATE: \"private\"}\n+\n+\n+def _request(specs, *, category=\"packages\", resolved_default_deps=None, pre=False):\n+    return ResolverRequest(\n+        schema_version=SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+        category=category,\n+        packages=PackageSpecs(specs=specs),\n+        options=ResolverOptions(backend=\"uv\", pre=pre),\n+        sources=(\n+            Source(name=\"pypi\", url=_PYPI),\n+            Source(name=\"private\", url=_PRIVATE, verify_ssl=False),\n+        ),\n+        python_marker_override=\"3.11.4\",\n+        resolved_default_deps=resolved_default_deps,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Registry / availability\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+class TestRegistry:\n+    def test_uv_is_registered(self):\n+        assert \"uv\" in list_backends()\n+        assert isinstance(get_backend(\"uv\"), UvBackend)\n+\n+    def test_is_available_follows_path_lookup(self):\n+        backend = UvBackend()\n+        with mock.patch.object(uv_backend.shutil, \"which\", return_value=\"/bin/uv\"):\n+            assert backend.is_available() is True\n+        with mock.patch.object(uv_backend.shutil, \"which\", return_value=None):\n+            assert backend.is_available() is False\n+\n+    def test_dispatcher_reports_install_hint_when_uv_missing(self):\n+        from pipenv.resolver.core import resolve_for_pipenv\n+\n+        with mock.patch.object(uv_backend.shutil, \"which\", return_value=None):\n+            response = resolve_for_pipenv(_request({\"six\": \"six\"}))\n+        assert isinstance(response.result, InternalError)\n+        assert \"uv was not found on $PATH\" in response.result.message\n+        assert \"pip install uv\" in response.result.message\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Spec translation\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+class TestParseSpec:\n+    def test_extras_and_markers(self):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"requests\",\n+            \"requests[socks]>=2.30; sys_platform == 'linux'\",\n+            None,\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.extras == (\"socks\",)\n+        assert dep.markers == \"sys_platform == 'linux'\"\n+        assert dep.specifier == \">=2.30\"\n+        assert dep.index is None\n+\n+    def test_index_flag_maps_to_source_name(self):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\"torch\", f\"torch -i {_PRIVATE}\", None, _URL_TO_NAME)\n+        assert dep.index == \"private\"\n+        assert dep.pep508 == \"torch\"\n+\n+    def test_index_flag_matches_source_with_credentials(self):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"torch\",\n+            \"torch -i https://user:secret@private.example.com/simple/\",\n+            None,\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.index == \"private\"\n+\n+    def test_lock_index_follows_pip_backend_rule(self):\n+        # Plain string Pipfile entry \u2192 records the index it resolves from.\n+        string_entry = _parse_spec(\"six\", \"six\", \"*\", _URL_TO_NAME)\n+        assert string_entry.lock_index == \"pypi\"\n+        # Dict entry without ``index`` \u2192 no ``index`` in the lockfile,\n+        # even though ``convert_deps_to_pip`` added ``-i <primary>``.\n+        dict_entry = _parse_spec(\n+            \"requests\", f\"requests -i {_PYPI}\", {\"version\": \"*\"}, _URL_TO_NAME\n+        )\n+        assert dict_entry.lock_index is None\n+        assert dict_entry.index == \"pypi\"\n+\n+    def test_vcs_spec(self):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"attrs\",\n+            \"attrs @ git+https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git@25.3.0#subdirectory=src\",\n+            {\"git\": \"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git\", \"editable\": True},\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.vcs.backend == \"git\"\n+        assert dep.vcs.url == \"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git\"\n+        assert dep.vcs.ref == \"25.3.0\"\n+        assert dep.vcs.subdirectory == \"src\"\n+        assert dep.editable is True\n+        assert dep.lock_index is None\n+\n+    def test_editable_path(self, tmp_path):\n+        pkg = tmp_path / \"localpkg\"\n+        pkg.mkdir()\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"localpkg\",\n+            f\"-e {pkg}\",\n+            {\"path\": \"./localpkg\", \"editable\": True},\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.editable is True\n+        assert dep.path == \"./localpkg\"\n+        assert dep.abs_path == str(pkg)\n+\n+    def test_editable_path_with_extras_and_markers(self, tmp_path):\n+        pkg = tmp_path / \"localpkg\"\n+        pkg.mkdir()\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"localpkg\",\n+            f\"-e {pkg}[test,docs]; sys_platform == 'linux'\",\n+            {\"path\": str(pkg), \"editable\": True},\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.abs_path == str(pkg)\n+        assert dep.extras == (\"docs\", \"test\")\n+        assert dep.markers == \"sys_platform == 'linux'\"\n+\n+    def test_non_editable_local_file_is_a_direct_reference(self, tmp_path):\n+        wheel = tmp_path / \"pkg-1.0-py3-none-any.whl\"\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"pkg\",\n+            f\"{wheel}[extra]; os_name == 'posix'\",\n+            {\"file\": str(wheel)},\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.pep508 == f\"pkg[extra] @ {wheel.as_uri()} ; os_name == 'posix'\"\n+        assert dep.file == str(wheel)\n+        assert dep.path is None\n+\n+    def test_package_named_like_a_local_directory_is_not_a_path(\n+        self, tmp_path, monkeypatch\n+    ):\n+        (tmp_path / \"flask\").mkdir()\n+        monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\"flask\", \"flask\", \"*\", _URL_TO_NAME)\n+        assert dep.abs_path is None\n+        assert dep.path is None\n+        assert dep.pep508 == \"flask\"\n+\n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+        \"spec, url, vcs\",\n+        [\n+            (\n+                \"pkg @ https://example.com/pkg-1.0.whl; os_name == 'posix'\",\n+                \"https://example.com/pkg-1.0.whl\",\n+                False,\n+            ),\n+            (\n+                \"pkg @ git+https://example.com/r.git@v1; os_name == 'posix'\",\n+                \"git+https://example.com/r.git@v1\",\n+                True,\n+            ),\n+        ],\n+    )\n+    def test_url_with_marker_and_no_space(self, spec, url, vcs):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\"pkg\", spec, None, _URL_TO_NAME)\n+        assert dep.markers == \"os_name == 'posix'\"\n+        assert dep.pep508.startswith(f\"pkg @ {url} ;\")\n+        assert bool(dep.vcs) is vcs\n+\n+    def test_legacy_local_vcs_spec(self):\n+        entry = {\n+            \"git\": \"file:///repo\",\n+            \"ref\": \"abc\",\n+            \"editable\": True,\n+            \"extras\": [\"x\"],\n+            \"subdirectory\": \"sub\",\n+            \"markers\": \"os_name == 'posix'\",\n+        }\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"pkg\",\n+            \"-e git+file:///repo@abc#egg=pkg&subdirectory=sub[x]\",\n+            entry,\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.pep508.startswith(\"pkg[x] @ git+file:///repo@abc#subdirectory=sub ;\")\n+        assert dep.vcs == VCSPin(\n+            backend=\"git\", url=\"file:///repo\", ref=\"abc\", subdirectory=\"sub\"\n+        )\n+        assert dep.extras == (\"x\",)\n+        assert dep.markers == \"os_name == 'posix'\"\n+        assert dep.editable is True\n+\n+    def test_legacy_vcs_editable_follows_pipfile(self):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"pkg\", \"-e git+file:///repo#egg=pkg\", {\"git\": \"file:///repo\"}, _URL_TO_NAME\n+        )\n+        assert dep.pep508 == \"pkg @ git+file:///repo\"\n+        assert dep.editable is False\n+\n+    def test_legacy_vcs_local_path_repository(self, tmp_path):\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\n+            \"pkg\",\n+            f\"-e git+{tmp_path}@abc#egg=pkg\",\n+            {\"git\": str(tmp_path), \"ref\": \"abc\"},\n+            _URL_TO_NAME,\n+        )\n+        assert dep.pep508 == f\"pkg @ git+{tmp_path.as_uri()}@abc\"\n+        assert dep.vcs.ref == \"abc\"\n+\n+    def test_remote_file(self):\n+        url = \"https://files.example.com/idna-3.20-py3-none-any.whl\"\n+        dep = _parse_spec(\"idna\", f\"idna @ {url}\", {\"file\": url}, _URL_TO_NAME)\n+        assert dep.file == url\n+        assert dep.abs_path is None\n+\n+    def test_vcs_pin_ssh_url_keeps_user(self):\n+        pin = _vcs_pin(\"git+ssh://git@github.com/org/repo.git@abc123\")\n+        assert pin.url == \"ssh://git@github.com/org/repo.git\"\n+        assert pin.ref == \"abc123\"\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Generated pyproject.toml\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+class TestRenderPyproject:\n+    def _render(self, specs, entries=None, pins=None):\n+        deps = [\n+            _parse_spec(name, spec, (entries or {}).get(name), _URL_TO_NAME)\n+            for name, spec in specs.items()\n+        ]\n+        index_pins = dict(pins or {})\n+        for dep in deps:\n+            if dep.index:\n+                index_pins[dep.name] = dep.index\n+        sources = [Source(name=\"pypi\", url=_PYPI), Source(name=\"private\", url=_PRIVATE)]\n+        return _render_pyproject(deps, sources, index_pins)\n+\n+    def test_non_primary_sources_are_explicit(self):\n+        text = self._render({\"six\": \"six\", \"torch\": f\"torch -i {_PRIVATE}\"})\n+        if tomllib is None:\n+            pytest.skip(\"tomllib unavailable\")\n+        data = tomllib.loads(text)\n+        # The primary index is passed as UV_DEFAULT_INDEX, not declared here.\n+        indexes = data[\"tool\"][\"uv\"][\"index\"]\n+        assert indexes == [{\"name\": \"private\", \"url\": _PRIVATE, \"explicit\": True}]\n+        sources = data[\"tool\"][\"uv\"][\"sources\"]\n+        assert sources == {\"torch\": {\"index\": \"private\"}}\n+        assert data[\"project\"][\"dependencies\"] == [\"six\", \"torch\"]\n+\n+    def test_pins_to_primary_are_omitted(self):\n+        text = self._render({\"requests\": f\"requests -i {_PYPI}\"})\n+        if tomllib is None:\n+            pytest.skip(\"tomllib unavailable\")\n+        assert tomllib.loads(text)[\"tool\"][\"uv\"].get(\"sources\", {}) == {}\n+\n+    def test_editable_path_becomes_path_source(self, tmp_path):\n+        pkg = tmp_path / \"localpkg\"\n+        pkg.mkdir()\n+        text = self._render(\n+            {\"localpkg\": f\"-e {pkg}\"},\n+            entries={\"localpkg\": {\"path\": str(pkg), \"editable\": True}},\n+        )\n+        if tomllib is None:\n+            pytest.skip(\"tomllib unavailable\")\n+        data = tomllib.loads(text)\n+        assert data[\"project\"][\"dependencies\"] == [\"localpkg\"]\n+        assert data[\"tool\"][\"uv\"][\"sources\"][\"localpkg\"] == {\n+            \"path\": str(pkg),\n+            \"editable\": True,\n+        }\n+\n+    def test_skip_resolver_entries_are_not_resolved(self):\n+        text = self._render(\n+            {\"six\": \"six\", \"odd\": \"odd\"}, entries={\"odd\": {\"skip_resolver\": True}}\n+        )\n+        if tomllib is None:\n+            pytest.skip(\"tomllib unavailable\")\n+        assert tomllib.loads(text)[\"project\"][\"dependencies\"] == [\"six\"]\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Output parsing and marker folding\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+_COMPILE_OUTPUT = \"\"\"\\\n+-e /work/localpkg\n+    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\n+attrs @ git+https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git@3dca08ce5bbe673d7df25f44f3dda92505d1043d\n+    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\n+pluggy==1.7.0 \\\\\n+    --hash=sha256:bbb \\\\\n+    --hash=sha256:aaa\n+    # via pytest\n+pytest==9.2.0 \\\\\n+    --hash=sha256:ccc\n+    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\n+six==1.17.0 \\\\\n+    --hash=sha256:ddd\n+    # via\n+    #   localpkg\n+    #   pytest\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+class TestParseCompileOutput:\n+    def test_blocks_hashes_and_via(self):\n+        entries = {e.line.split(\"==\")[0]: e for e in _parse_compile_output(_COMPILE_OUTPUT)}\n+        assert entries[\"pluggy\"].hashes == [\"sha256:bbb\", \"sha256:aaa\"]\n+        assert entries[\"pluggy\"].via == [\"pytest\"]\n+        assert entries[\"six\"].via == [\"localpkg\", \"pytest\"]\n+        assert entries[\"-e /work/localpkg\"].via == [\"your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\"]\n+\n+\n+class TestFoldMarkers:\n+    def _deps(self, **markers):\n+        return {\n+            name: mock.Mock(markers=marker)\n+            for name, marker in markers.items()\n+        }\n+\n+    def test_marker_guarded_root_propagates(self):\n+        parents = {\"pytest\": {\"\"}, \"pluggy\": {\"pytest\"}}\n+        folded = _fold_markers(parents, self._deps(pytest=\"sys_platform == 'linux'\"))\n+        assert folded[\"pluggy\"] == \"sys_platform == 'linux'\"\n+\n+    def test_unconditional_path_wins(self):\n+        parents = {\"a\": {\"\"}, \"b\": {\"\"}, \"shared\": {\"a\", \"b\"}}\n+        folded = _fold_markers(parents, self._deps(a=\"os_name == 'nt'\", b=None))\n+        assert folded[\"shared\"] is None\n+\n+    def test_alternative_markers_are_ored(self):\n+        parents = {\"a\": {\"\"}, \"b\": {\"\"}, \"shared\": {\"a\", \"b\"}}\n+        folded = _fold_markers(\n+            parents, self._deps(a=\"os_name == 'nt'\", b=\"sys_platform == 'darwin'\")\n+        )\n+        assert folded[\"shared\"] == \"(os_name == 'nt') or (sys_platform == 'darwin')\"\n+\n+    def test_cycle_through_other_root_keeps_every_marker(self):\n+        parents = {\"a\": {\"\", \"b\"}, \"b\": {\"c\"}, \"c\": {\"a\", \"d\"}, \"d\": {\"\"}}\n+        folded = _fold_markers(\n+            parents, self._deps(a=\"os_name == 'posix'\", d=\"os_name == 'nt'\")\n+        )\n+        both = \"(os_name == 'nt') or (os_name == 'posix')\"\n+        assert folded[\"a\"] == both\n+        assert folded[\"b\"] == both\n+        assert folded[\"c\"] == both\n+        assert folded[\"d\"] == \"os_name == 'nt'\"\n+\n+    def test_cycles_terminate(self):\n+        parents = {\"a\": {\"\", \"b\"}, \"b\": {\"a\"}}\n+        folded = _fold_markers(parents, self._deps(a=\"os_name == 'nt'\"))\n+        assert folded[\"b\"] == \"os_name == 'nt'\"\n+\n+\n+class TestUnneededPinOnly:\n+    def test_unused_pin_and_its_dependencies_are_unneeded(self):\n+        parents = {\"app\": {\"\"}, \"pinned\": {\"\"}, \"helper\": {\"pinned\"}}\n+        assert _unneeded_pin_only(parents, frozenset({\"pinned\"})) == {\n+            \"pinned\",\n+            \"helper\",\n+        }\n+\n+    def test_used_pin_is_kept_without_its_root_edge(self):\n+        parents = {\"app\": {\"\"}, \"pinned\": {\"\", \"app\"}, \"helper\": {\"pinned\"}}\n+        assert _unneeded_pin_only(parents, frozenset({\"pinned\"})) == set()\n+        assert parents[\"pinned\"] == {\"app\"}\n+\n+    def test_cycle_among_unused_pins_is_unneeded(self):\n+        parents = {\"app\": {\"\"}, \"x\": {\"\", \"y\"}, \"y\": {\"x\"}}\n+        assert _unneeded_pin_only(parents, frozenset({\"x\"})) == {\"x\", \"y\"}\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# End-to-end resolve() with the uv subprocess mocked\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _run_resolve(request, *, stdout=\"\", stderr=\"\", returncode=0, pipfile=({}, {})):\n+    completed = subprocess.CompletedProcess([], returncode, stdout=stdout, stderr=stderr)\n+    with mock.patch.object(uv_backend.shutil, \"which\", return_value=\"/usr/bin/uv\"), \\\n+            mock.patch.object(uv_backend, \"_pipfile_context\", return_value=pipfile), \\\n+            mock.patch.object(uv_backend.subprocess, \"run\", return_value=completed) as run:\n+        response = UvBackend().resolve(request)\n+    return response, run\n+\n+\n+class TestResolve:\n+    def test_success_translates_entries(self, tmp_path):\n+        pkg = tmp_path / \"localpkg\"\n+        pkg.mkdir()\n+        output = _COMPILE_OUTPUT.replace(\"/work/localpkg\", str(pkg))\n+        request = _request(\n+            {\n+                \"localpkg\": f\"-e {pkg}\",\n+                \"attrs\": \"attrs @ git+https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git@25.3.0\",\n+                \"pytest\": f\"pytest; sys_platform == 'linux' -i {_PYPI}\",\n+                \"colorama\": f\"colorama; sys_platform == 'win32' -i {_PYPI}\",\n+            }\n+        )\n+        entries = {\n+            \"localpkg\": {\"path\": \"./localpkg\", \"editable\": True},\n+            \"pytest\": {\"version\": \"*\", \"markers\": \"sys_platform == 'linux'\"},\n+            \"colorama\": {\"version\": \"*\", \"markers\": \"sys_platform == 'win32'\"},\n+        }\n+        response, run = _run_resolve(request, stdout=output, pipfile=(entries, {}))\n+\n+        assert isinstance(response.result, ResolverSuccess), response.result\n+        locked = {entry.name: entry for entry in response.result.locked}\n+        assert locked[\"localpkg\"].path == \"./localpkg\"\n+        assert locked[\"localpkg\"].editable is True\n+        assert locked[\"attrs\"].vcs.ref == \"3dca08ce5bbe673d7df25f44f3dda92505d1043d\"\n+        assert locked[\"pytest\"].version == \"==9.2.0\"\n+        assert locked[\"pytest\"].markers == \"sys_platform == 'linux'\"\n+        assert locked[\"pytest\"].hashes == (\"sha256:ccc\",)\n+        assert locked[\"pluggy\"].markers == \"sys_platform == 'linux'\"\n+        assert locked[\"pluggy\"].hashes == (\"sha256:aaa\", \"sha256:bbb\")\n+        # ``six`` is needed unconditionally via localpkg.\n+        assert locked[\"six\"].markers is None\n+        # colorama doesn't apply to this environment; recorded like the\n+        # pip backend does (no hashes, original specifier).\n+        assert locked[\"colorama\"] == LockedRequirement(\n+            name=\"colorama\", version=\"*\", markers=\"sys_platform == 'win32'\"\n+        )\n+\n+        cmd = run.call_args.args[0]\n+        assert cmd[:3] == [\"/usr/bin/uv\", \"pip\", \"compile\"]\n+        assert \"--generate-hashes\" in cmd\n+        assert cmd[cmd.index(\"--python-version\") + 1] == \"3.11.4\"\n+        assert cmd[cmd.index(\"--allow-insecure-host\") + 1] == \"private.example.com\"\n+        assert cmd[cmd.index(\"--prerelease\") + 1] == \"explicit\"\n+\n+    def test_resolved_default_deps_become_constraints(self):\n+        resolved = ResolvedDeps(\n+            entries=(\n+                LockedRequirement(name=\"six\", version=\"==1.17.0\"),\n+                LockedRequirement(name=\"colorama\", version=\"*\"),\n+            )\n+        )\n+        request = _request({\"pytest\": \"pytest\"}, category=\"dev-packages\",\n+                           resolved_default_deps=resolved, pre=True)\n+        captured = {}\n+\n+        def fake_run(cmd, **kwargs):\n+            path = cmd[cmd.index(\"--constraint\") + 1]\n+            with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n+                captured[\"constraints\"] = fh.read()\n+            return subprocess.CompletedProcess(cmd, 0, stdout=\"\", stderr=\"\")\n+\n+        with mock.patch.object(uv_backend.shutil, \"which\", return_value=\"/usr/bin/uv\"), \\\n+                mock.patch.object(uv_backend, \"_pipfile_context\", return_value=({}, {})), \\\n+                mock.patch.object(uv_backend.subprocess, \"run\", side_effect=fake_run):\n+            UvBackend().resolve(request)\n+        assert captured[\"constraints\"] == \"six==1.17.0\\n\"\n+\n+    def test_resolved_vcs_constraint_keeps_subdirectory(self):\n+        request = _request(\n+            {\"six\": \"six\"},\n+            category=\"dev-packages\",\n+            resolved_default_deps=ResolvedDeps(\n+                entries=(\n+                    LockedRequirement(\n+                        name=\"pkg\",\n+                        vcs=VCSPin(\n+                            backend=\"git\",\n+                            url=\"https://example.com/r.git\",\n+                            ref=\"abc\",\n+                            subdirectory=\"sub\",\n+                        ),\n+                    ),\n+                )\n+            ),\n+        )\n+        assert _render_constraints(request) == (\n+            \"pkg @ git+https://example.com/r.git@abc#subdirectory=sub\\n\"\n+        )\n+\n+    def test_foreign_pin_is_required_then_dropped_when_unused(self):\n+        captured = {}\n+\n+        def fake_run(cmd, **kwargs):\n+            captured[\"pyproject\"] = Path(cmd[3]).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+            return mock.Mock(\n+                returncode=0,\n+                stderr=\"\",\n+                stdout=(\n+                    \"app==1.0\\n    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\\n\"\n+                    \"helper==1.0\\n    # via pinned\\n\"\n+                    \"pinned==1.0\\n    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\\n\"\n+                ),\n+            )\n+\n+        with mock.patch(\"shutil.which\", return_value=\"/usr/bin/uv\"), mock.patch(\n+            \"pipenv.resolver.backends.uv._pipfile_context\",\n+            return_value=({}, {\"pinned\": \"private\"}),\n+        ), mock.patch(\"subprocess.run\", side_effect=fake_run):\n+            response = UvBackend().resolve(\n+                _request({\"app\": \"app\"}, category=\"dev-packages\")\n+            )\n+        assert '\"pinned\",' in captured[\"pyproject\"]\n+        assert '\"pinned\" = { index = \"private\" }' in captured[\"pyproject\"]\n+        assert [r.name for r in response.result.locked] == [\"app\"]\n+\n+    def test_foreign_pin_used_transitively_is_locked_with_its_index(self):\n+        stdout = (\n+            \"app==1.0\\n    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\\n\"\n+            \"pinned==1.0\\n    # via\\n\"\n+            \"    #   your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\\n    #   app\\n\"\n+        )\n+        with mock.patch(\"shutil.which\", return_value=\"/usr/bin/uv\"), mock.patch(\n+            \"pipenv.resolver.backends.uv._pipfile_context\",\n+            return_value=({}, {\"pinned\": \"private\"}),\n+        ), mock.patch(\n+            \"subprocess.run\",\n+            return_value=mock.Mock(returncode=0, stderr=\"\", stdout=stdout),\n+        ):\n+            response = UvBackend().resolve(\n+                _request({\"app\": \"app\"}, category=\"dev-packages\")\n+            )\n+        locked = {r.name: r for r in response.result.locked}\n+        assert locked[\"pinned\"].index == \"private\"\n+        assert locked[\"pinned\"].version == \"==1.0\"\n+\n+    def test_non_editable_path_output_line_has_no_name(self, tmp_path):\n+        pkg = tmp_path / \"localpkg\"\n+        pkg.mkdir()\n+        entries = {\"localpkg\": {\"path\": str(pkg)}}\n+        stdout = f\"{pkg}\\n    # via your-pipfile (pyproject.toml)\\n\"\n+        response, _ = _run_resolve(\n+            _request({\"localpkg\": str(pkg)}), stdout=stdout, pipfile=(entries, {})\n+        )\n+        locked = response.result.locked\n+        assert [r.name for r in locked] == [\"localpkg\"]\n+        assert locked[0].path == str(pkg)\n+\n+    def test_exit_1_is_resolution_error(self):\n+        response, _ = _run_resolve(\n+            _request({\"six\": \"six\"}),\n+            returncode=1,\n+            stderr=\"  \u00d7 No solution found when resolving dependencies\",\n+        )\n+        assert isinstance(response.result, ResolutionError)\n+        assert \"No solution found\" in response.result.pip_message\n+\n+    def test_other_exit_is_internal_error(self):\n+        response, _ = _run_resolve(\n+            _request({\"six\": \"six\"}), returncode=2, stderr=\"error: unexpected argument\"\n+        )\n+        assert isinstance(response.result, InternalError)\n+        assert \"unexpected argument\" in response.result.message\n+\n+    def test_missing_binary_is_internal_error(self):\n+        with mock.patch.object(uv_backend.shutil, \"which\", return_value=None):\n+            response = UvBackend().resolve(_request({\"six\": \"six\"}))\n+        assert isinstance(response.result, InternalError)\n+        assert \"uv was not found\" in response.result.message\n+\n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+        \"variable\", [\"UV_NO_SOURCES\", \"UV_NO_SOURCES_PACKAGE\", \"UV_TORCH_BACKEND\"]\n+    )\n+    def test_source_overriding_variables_are_scrubbed(self, monkeypatch, variable):\n+        monkeypatch.setenv(variable, \"1\")\n+        assert variable not in _uv_environment(\"https://pypi.org/simple\")\n+\n+    def test_primary_index_is_uv_default_index(self, monkeypatch):\n+        monkeypatch.setenv(\"UV_INDEX_URL\", \"https://evil.example.com/simple\")\n+        monkeypatch.setenv(\"UV_DEFAULT_INDEX\", \"https://evil.example.com/simple\")\n+        monkeypatch.setenv(\"PIP_KEYRING_PROVIDER\", \"auto\")\n+        monkeypatch.delenv(\"UV_KEYRING_PROVIDER\", raising=False)\n+        _, run = _run_resolve(_request({\"six\": \"six\"}))\n+        env = run.call_args.kwargs[\"env\"]\n+        assert \"UV_INDEX_URL\" not in env\n+        assert env[\"UV_DEFAULT_INDEX\"] == _PYPI\n+        # Never on the command line, where credentials would be visible.\n+        assert _PYPI not in run.call_args.args[0]\n+        assert env[\"UV_KEYRING_PROVIDER\"] == \"subprocess\"\n", "problem_statement": "Accelerate build times by using uv instead of pip?\nThere is a lot of discussion about the Rust-based `pip`-replacement named `uv`.\r\n* https://astral.sh/blog/uv\r\n* https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/blob/main/README.md\r\n\r\nWould it be of interest to accelerate `pipenv` build times by using `uv` instead of `pip`?\r\n\r\n### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\r\n\r\nI'm always frustrated when pipenv builds take several minutes.\r\n\r\n### Describe the solution you'd like\r\n\r\npipenv builds take seconds instead of minutes.\r\n\r\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\r\n\r\nSwitch to non-pipenv solutions for our builds.\n", "hints_text": "I am stuck on the philosophical questions of: would we need to rebrand to uvenv?   maybe it should be a whole new project -- but is it realistically much faster when most things are network activity of getting the wheels, and then they still need to be installed?   In all seriousness though, it might be worth me  taking a deeper look, but we have to admit that pipenv is a big bear hug around pip and so there is a lot to detangle there if there were a motivation to wrap a different package library.\nThe caching in uv is super impressive.  The first build is lightning fast but the second is astonishing especially on a huge set of deps.\n+1 for supporting `uv`\nIt's been a good ride, but `uv` has far surpassed pipenv. Unfortunately this is what historically happens to ~~open source~~ software projects, something evolutionary comes along and kills old solutions.\nuv is still pre v1.0, but since August 20 has fully replaced my Pipenv workflow with the implementation of their lock file.\r\nhttps://astral.sh/blog/uv-unified-python-packaging\nLanguages like Go and Rust have quite a different approach to reaching v1.0 than Python does.  Once a package has reached v1.0 in these languages it is kind of a commitment to Never break backward compatibility.  There is no such commitment w/ Python packages.\nI made POC pipenv-uv, a package that monkey patches pipenv's resolver and installer with uv's.  @matteius would having uv be an alternative resolver be a feature you would consider.\n\n[github.com/FlavioAmurrioCS/pipenv-uv](https://github.com/FlavioAmurrioCS/pipenv-uv)\n\nInspiration: https://pypi.org/project/pre-commit-uv/\n@FlavioAmurrioCS actually yes, I would -- it was something I was thinking about a couple months back, but it could not repalce -- serve as an alternative, I may have branch floating around somewhere too.   Problem is I won't have time to look into this specifically for a bit.  I do hope to vendor in latest pip and do a few other updates soon, but this is a much bigger change.\n\nSee my priror research:  https://github.com/pypa/pipenv/pull/new/uv-backend\nCool! I have gotten pretty close to parity with original pipenv functionality since I still wanted to keep Pipfile.lock and have people/CI using old pipenv to still work. For my approach I use `uv pip compile` to resolve into a requirements.txt and I was parsing that (this was before pylock.toml). I'll check if I can move pylock.toml to make it easier. I'll fork, patch, see if all test pass and then move to a proper implementation.\n\n\nUpdate, I have a POC working. Will give it to some coworkers to test it out before making the PR.\nUpdate on this?\npipenv now has a pluggable resolver system -- there are two resolver to choose from, the pip resolver and now a faster pure-python resolver (well mostly faster, it will be totally faster when #6739 gets merged).   This opens the door to better supporting other resolvers too.", "created_at": "2026-10-29T08:17:12Z"}
{"repo": "pypa/pipenv", "pull_number": 6769, "instance_id": "pypa__pipenv-6769", "issue_numbers": ["6661"], "base_commit": "5bba154db51ea552c219caa212cf1e13097de00b", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/_templates/hacks.html b/docs/_templates/hacks.html\nindex 00c88843ca..e3da6ec949 100644\n--- a/docs/_templates/hacks.html\n+++ b/docs/_templates/hacks.html\n@@ -1,4 +1,3 @@\n-<script type=\"text/javascript\">$('#searchbox').hide(0);</script>\n <!--Alabaster (krTheme++) Hacks -->\n \n <!-- CSS Adjustments (I'm very picky.) -->\n@@ -7,9 +6,6 @@\n   /* Rezzy requires precise alignment. */\n   img.logo {margin-left: -20px!important;}\n \n-  /* \"Quick Search\" should be not be shown for now. */\n-  div#searchbox h3 {display: none;}\n-\n   /* Make the document a little wider, less code is cut-off. */\n   div.document {width: 1008px;}\n \ndiff --git a/docs/_templates/sidebarlogo.html b/docs/_templates/sidebarlogo.html\nindex 20a3cf0b8e..4670b72f79 100644\n--- a/docs/_templates/sidebarlogo.html\n+++ b/docs/_templates/sidebarlogo.html\n@@ -1,29 +1,11 @@\n-<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/docsearch.js@2/dist/cdn/docsearch.min.css\" />\n <style>\n-  .algolia-autocomplete{\n-    width: 100%;\n-    height: 1.5em\n-  }\n-  .algolia-autocomplete a{\n-    border-bottom: none !important;\n-  }\n   iframe.noScrolling{\n     overflow: hidden;\n   }\n   iframe.noBorder{\n     border: none;\n   }\n-  #doc_search{\n-    width: 100%;\n-    height: 100%;\n-  }\n-  </style>\n-  <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/docsearch.js@2/dist/cdn/docsearch.min.js\" onload=\"docsearch({\n-    apiKey: '0dbb76467f0c180a1344fc46858df17b',\n-    indexName: 'pipenv',\n-    inputSelector: '#doc_search',\n-    debug: false // Set debug to true if you want to inspect the dropdown\n-  })\" async></script>\n+</style>\n <p class=\"logo\">\n   <a href=\"{{ pathto(master_doc) }}\">\n     <img class=\"logo\" src=\"{{ pathto('_static/pipenv.png', 1) }}\" title=\"Gift-wrapped box w/ 'pipenv' on the ribbon\"/>\n@@ -34,7 +16,7 @@\n   <iframe src=\"https://ghbtns.com/github-btn.html?user=pypa&repo=pipenv&type=watch&count=true&size=large\"\n     allowtransparency=\"true\" class=\"noScrolling noBorder\" width=\"200px\" height=\"35px\" ></iframe>\n </p>\n-<input id=\"doc_search\" label=\"doc_search\" placeholder=\"Search the doc\" autofocus/>\n+{% include \"searchbox.html\" %}\n <p>\n   <strong>Pipenv</strong> is a production-ready tool that aims to bring the best of all packaging worlds to the Python world. It harnesses Pipfile, pip, and virtualenv into one single command.\n   <p>It features very pretty terminal colors.</p>\ndiff --git a/docs/conf.py b/docs/conf.py\nindex c8bc5ac6c8..69d9d519a7 100644\n--- a/docs/conf.py\n+++ b/docs/conf.py\n@@ -122,14 +122,14 @@\n     \"show_related\": False,\n }\n \n+# sidebarlogo.html includes the search box near the top of the sidebar.\n html_sidebars = {\n-    \"index\": [\"sidebarlogo.html\", \"sourcelink.html\", \"searchbox.html\", \"hacks.html\"],\n+    \"index\": [\"sidebarlogo.html\", \"sourcelink.html\", \"hacks.html\"],\n     \"**\": [\n         \"sidebarlogo.html\",\n         \"localtoc.html\",\n         \"relations.html\",\n         \"sourcelink.html\",\n-        \"searchbox.html\",\n         \"hacks.html\",\n     ],\n }\ndiff --git a/news/6661.doc.rst b/news/6661.doc.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..d1cf202b63\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/6661.doc.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\n+Replace the documentation's outdated Algolia search with Sphinx's built-in search,\n+so results point to pages in the documentation version being viewed.\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Search bar broken on RTD page for valid results\n### Issue description\n\nThe search bar on the [RTD page](https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/quick_start.html) is broken when queried for a valid result (the page seems to block invalid results, e.g., \"foobar\").\n\n### Expected result\n\nOne or more results should be returned or a page stating there are no results should be displayed.\n\n### Actual result\n\nSee the screenshot below.\n\n<img width=\"656\" height=\"617\" alt=\"404-documentation-not-found-screenshot\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3edc6e43-4c9a-4610-8b79-f20c4d326c8f\" />\n\n### Steps to Replicate\n\n- Go to the [RTD page](https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/quick_start.html).\n- In the \"search the doc\" text field, enter in `python_version` (for example).\n- Either press Enter or pick one of the autofilled results.\n\nAn example screenshot is included below:\n\n<img width=\"227\" height=\"230\" alt=\"python_version-suggestion\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6b3df9b-d502-4486-a1f2-568503ae2de7\" />\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-29T06:15:04Z"}
{"repo": "pypa/pipenv", "pull_number": 6768, "instance_id": "pypa__pipenv-6768", "issue_numbers": ["6759"], "base_commit": "f9dc02e612f9f72f5086fa81fe459e4d701fb933", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/pylock.md b/docs/pylock.md\nindex 6c58d70bd..8aee78675 100644\n--- a/docs/pylock.md\n+++ b/docs/pylock.md\n@@ -118,8 +118,9 @@ pipenv pylock --generate --output /path/to/pylock.toml\n ### Custom Dependency Groups\n \n Custom Pipfile categories such as `[lint]` and `[docs]` are exported with their\n-own dependency group names. Reading a pylock file restores those names as\n-separate categories. The `dev` group maps to `dev-packages` (`develop` in\n+own dependency group names, normalized as PEP 735 requires (`[My_Docs]` becomes\n+`my-docs`). Pipenv records the original category of each group under\n+`[tool.pipenv.categories]`, so reading the file restores the same categories. The `dev` group maps to `dev-packages` (`develop` in\n `Pipfile.lock`); `--dev` does not enable every custom group.\n \n ```bash\n@@ -137,8 +138,11 @@ Use `--dev-groups` to label develop packages with alternative group names:\n pipenv pylock --generate --dev-groups \"dev,test,docs\"\n ```\n \n-Those packages can then be selected through any of the named groups. Custom\n-Pipfile categories are exported automatically, independently of this option.\n+Other installers can then select those packages through any of the named\n+groups; Pipenv reads them back as `dev-packages`. Custom Pipfile categories are\n+exported automatically, independently of this option. Generation fails if two\n+categories, or a category and one of the `--dev-groups`, normalize to the same\n+group name.\n Shared dependencies retain each category's environment markers during conversion.\n \n ## pyproject.toml Support\ndiff --git a/news/6759.bugfix.rst b/news/6759.bugfix.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..7a2ee3a47\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/6759.bugfix.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\n+Normalize the dependency group names written to ``pylock.toml`` and record each group's original category under ``[tool.pipenv.categories]`` so reading the file restores the same categories, including ``--dev-groups`` aliases as ``develop``.\n+Generating ``pylock.toml`` now fails when two categories, or a category and one of the ``--dev-groups``, map to the same dependency group, instead of merging them.\ndiff --git a/pipenv/utils/pylock.py b/pipenv/utils/pylock.py\nindex 2de65d566..8f72817d6 100644\n--- a/pipenv/utils/pylock.py\n+++ b/pipenv/utils/pylock.py\n@@ -98,12 +98,26 @@ def from_lockfile(\n         except Exception as e:\n             raise ValueError(f\"Invalid Pipfile.lock file: {e}\")\n \n+        from pipenv.patched.pip._vendor.packaging.utils import canonicalize_name\n+\n+        # Group names are PEP 735 normalized; category names are not, so\n+        # record which category each group came from for the way back.\n+        dev_groups = list(dict.fromkeys(canonicalize_name(group) for group in dev_groups))\n         category_groups = {\"default\": [\"default\"], \"develop\": dev_groups}\n-        category_groups.update(\n-            (section, [section])\n-            for section in lockfile_data\n-            if section not in {\"_meta\", \"default\", \"develop\"}\n-        )\n+        group_categories = {\"default\": \"default\"}\n+        for section in dict.fromkeys([\"develop\", *lockfile_data]):\n+            if section in {\"_meta\", \"default\"}:\n+                continue\n+            groups = category_groups.setdefault(section, [canonicalize_name(section)])\n+            for group in groups:\n+                owner = group_categories.setdefault(group, section)\n+                if owner != section:\n+                    raise ValueError(\n+                        f\"Pipfile.lock categories {owner!r} and {section!r} both \"\n+                        f\"map to the dependency group {group!r}; rename the \"\n+                        \"category or choose different --dev-groups\"\n+                    )\n+        del group_categories[\"default\"]\n \n         # Create the basic pylock.toml structure\n         pylock_data: Dict[str, Any] = {\n@@ -243,6 +257,7 @@ def from_lockfile(\n                 \"generation_date\": datetime.datetime.now(\n                     datetime.timezone.utc\n                 ).isoformat(),\n+                \"categories\": group_categories,\n             }\n         }\n \n@@ -864,10 +879,17 @@ def _category_groups(self) -> Dict[str, Set[str]]:\n         for package in self.packages:\n             for group in sorted(_marker_dependency_groups(package.get(\"marker\"))):\n                 names.setdefault(group, group)\n+        # Pipenv records the category each group was exported from.\n+        recorded = self.tool.get(\"pipenv\", {}).get(\"categories\", {})\n+        if not isinstance(recorded, dict):\n+            recorded = {}\n+        recorded = {canonicalize_name(group): category for group, category in recorded.items()}\n         for group, name in names.items():\n             if group in defaults:\n                 continue\n-            category = \"develop\" if group in {\"dev\", \"develop\", \"dev-packages\"} else name\n+            category = recorded.get(group) or (\n+                \"develop\" if group in {\"dev\", \"develop\", \"dev-packages\"} else name\n+            )\n             categories.setdefault(category, set()).add(group)\n         return categories\n \n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/unit/test_pylock_categories.py b/tests/unit/test_pylock_categories.py\nindex 1238833ce..9c2948df8 100644\n--- a/tests/unit/test_pylock_categories.py\n+++ b/tests/unit/test_pylock_categories.py\n@@ -207,3 +207,46 @@ def test_lock_data_keeps_unselected_pylock_categories(tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n     assert list(lockfile[\"default\"]) == [\"runtime\"]\n     assert list(lockfile[\"develop\"]) == [\"devonly\"]\n     assert list(lockfile[\"lint\"]) == [\"lintonly\"]\n+\n+\n+def _lockfile(tmp_path, sections):\n+    data = {\"_meta\": {\"sources\": [], \"requires\": {}}, \"default\": {}, \"develop\": {}, **sections}\n+    path = tmp_path / \"Pipfile.lock\"\n+    path.write_text(json.dumps(data))\n+    return path\n+\n+\n+def test_export_normalizes_group_names_and_restores_categories(tmp_path):\n+    path = _lockfile(tmp_path, {\n+        \"develop\": {\"pytest\": {\"version\": \"==9.0\"}},\n+        \"My_Docs\": {\"sphinx\": {\"version\": \"==8.0\"}},\n+    })\n+\n+    pylock = PylockFile.from_lockfile(path, dev_groups=[\"dev\", \"Test\"])\n+    pylock.write()\n+    loaded = PylockFile.from_path(pylock.path)\n+\n+    assert loaded.dependency_groups == [\"dev\", \"test\", \"my-docs\"]\n+    assert [pkg[\"marker\"] for pkg in loaded.packages] == [\n+        \"'dev' in dependency_groups or 'test' in dependency_groups\",\n+        \"'my-docs' in dependency_groups\",\n+    ]\n+    converted = loaded.convert_to_pipenv_lockfile(environment=PY312)\n+    # The --dev-groups alias reads back as develop, not as a \"test\" category.\n+    assert sorted(key for key in converted if key != \"_meta\") == [\"My_Docs\", \"default\", \"develop\"]\n+    assert list(converted[\"develop\"]) == [\"pytest\"]\n+    assert list(converted[\"My_Docs\"]) == [\"sphinx\"]\n+    assert loaded.groups_for_categories([\"My_Docs\"]) == {\"my-docs\"}\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"sections, dev_groups\", [\n+    ({\"docs\": {}}, [\"dev\", \"docs\"]),\n+    ({\"dev\": {}}, None),\n+    ({\"my_docs\": {}, \"My-Docs\": {}}, None),\n+    ({}, [\"default\"]),\n+])\n+def test_export_rejects_categories_sharing_a_group(tmp_path, sections, dev_groups):\n+    path = _lockfile(tmp_path, sections)\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"both map to the dependency group\"):\n+        PylockFile.from_lockfile(path, dev_groups=dev_groups)\n", "problem_statement": "pylock.toml generation silently drops packages in custom Pipfile.lock categories\n### Problem\n`PylockFile.from_lockfile` (`pipenv/utils/pylock.py`) only walks the `default` and `develop` sections of `Pipfile.lock`. A project that uses its own categories (`pipenv install --categories docs sphinx`) therefore gets a `pylock.toml` without those packages. Nothing warns about it.\n\nReproduction with a `Pipfile.lock` containing `default: {requests}`, `develop: {pytest}`, `docs: {sphinx}`:\n\n```python\nfrom pipenv.utils.pylock import PylockFile\np = PylockFile.from_lockfile(\"Pipfile.lock\", \"pylock.toml\")\n[x[\"name\"] for x in p.data[\"packages\"]]   # ['requests', 'pytest']  (sphinx is gone)\np.data[\"dependency-groups\"]               # ['dev']\n```\n\nThis applies to `use_pylock` locking and to `pipenv pylock --generate`.\n\n### Why a fix needs a decision first\nThe natural PEP 751 mapping is one dependency group per category: write each custom category with a `'docs' in dependency_groups` marker and list `docs` in `dependency-groups`. But the reverse conversion (`convert_to_pipenv_lockfile`) only treats a marker as develop when it contains \"dev\" or \"test\"; a `'docs'` marker would be read back as a `default` package, so a docs-only dependency would end up installed everywhere. A correct fix therefore touches both directions. (#6758 already keeps such packages out of `default` on the read side by mapping any group other than the default one to `develop`; a per-category round trip would go one step further.)\n\n### Open question\nWould you accept this approach?\n1. Write: every extra category becomes a dependency group (name = category), with the same marker form used for `dev`.\n2. Read: take group names from the `dependency_groups` markers, map the configured dev group(s) to `develop`, and every other group back to a category of the same name.\n\nOr would you rather have only a warning for now when categories are skipped? I can send a PR for whichever you prefer, with tests for both directions.\n\nThis issue was drafted with AI assistance (Claude Code).\n\n", "hints_text": "Thanks for checking before writing it. Please go with the per-category round trip (1 + 2) rather than a warning. Categories are effectively dependency groups, and a `use_pylock` file that silently drops packages is worse than one that errors.\n\nPlease also move the read-side group handling from #6758 into this PR and narrow #6758 to the `requires-python` fix, so the classification logic lives in one place. Things to cover:\n\n- **Normalization:** group names follow PEP 735 normalization, but category names are arbitrary. Write the normalized name and keep the original category under `[tool.pipenv]` so the round trip gives back the same name.\n- **Collisions:** a category with the same name as one of the `--dev-groups` should be an error, not a silent merge.\n- **Shared packages:** extend `_merge_develop_marker` to N sections (OR each section's condition), and on read put a package in every category whose group selects it.\n- **Read side:** decide membership by evaluating the marker for each group (that group plus the default groups) rather than with a regex, and remove the `\"dev\"`/`\"test\"` substring heuristic.\n- **Install:** make sure `pipenv install --categories docs` from a pylock selects `dependency_groups={\"docs\"}`.\n- **Tests:** a Pipfile.lock \u2192 pylock \u2192 Pipfile.lock round trip that gives the same sections, including a package shared across categories with different markers.\n", "created_at": "2026-10-29T06:02:27Z"}
{"repo": "pypa/pipenv", "pull_number": 6749, "instance_id": "pypa__pipenv-6749", "issue_numbers": ["6748"], "base_commit": "56c31ad1a187d455e3b455e1c4a5ce1c757f9417", "patch": "diff --git a/MANIFEST.in b/MANIFEST.in\nindex ba859608d..bdbb88e35 100644\n--- a/MANIFEST.in\n+++ b/MANIFEST.in\n@@ -29,6 +29,11 @@ include tests/__init__.py\n include tests/conftest.py\n recursive-include tests/unit *.py\n \n+# tests/unit/test_release_tasks.py imports the top-level `tasks` package, so it\n+# must ship in the sdist too (it stays excluded from the installed packages).\n+# See: https://github.com/pypa/pipenv/issues/6748\n+recursive-include tasks *.py\n+\n prune .azure-pipelines\n prune .github\n prune pipenv/vendor/importlib_metadata/tests\ndiff --git a/news/6748.bugfix.rst b/news/6748.bugfix.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..b7bf23d01\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/6748.bugfix.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+Include the top-level ``tasks`` package in the sdist so that the shipped ``tests/unit/test_release_tasks.py`` can import it when the test suite is run from a source distribution.\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "[Testing] sdist is missing `tasks`\nThe sdist is missing `tasks` and so the testing fails:\n```\n============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform sunos5 -- Python 3.14.8, pytest-9.1.1, pluggy-1.7.0 -- /usr/bin/python3.14\ncachedir: .pytest_cache\nrootdir: /data/builds/ul-mass-rebuild/components/python/pipenv/build/amd64-3.14\nconfigfile: pyproject.toml\ncollecting ... collected 1169 items / 1 error\n\n==================================== ERRORS ====================================\n______________ ERROR collecting tests/unit/test_release_tasks.py _______________\nImportError while importing test module '/data/builds/ul-mass-rebuild/components/python/pipenv/build/amd64-3.14/tests/unit/test_release_tasks.py'.\nHint: make sure your test modules/packages have valid Python names.\nTraceback:\n/usr/lib/python3.14/importlib/__init__.py:88: in import_module\n    return _bootstrap._gcd_import(name[level:], package, level)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\ntests/unit/test_release_tasks.py:4: in <module>\n    from tasks import release as release_tasks\nE   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tasks'\n=============================== warnings summary ===============================\n../../../../../../../../usr/lib/python3.14/vendor-packages/_pytest/config/__init__.py:1464\n  /usr/lib/python3.14/vendor-packages/_pytest/config/__init__.py:1464: PytestConfigWarning: Unknown config option: plugins\n\n    self._warn_or_fail_if_strict(f\"Unknown config option: {key}\\n\")\n\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nERROR tests/unit/test_release_tasks.py\n!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! stopping after 1 failures !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n========================= 1 warning, 1 error in 3.00s ==========================\n```\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-19T21:58:35Z"}
{"repo": "pypa/pipenv", "pull_number": 6747, "instance_id": "pypa__pipenv-6747", "issue_numbers": ["5792"], "base_commit": "efb975dbefd663f5711dde2d4a30aef4f95a96a4", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/commands.md b/docs/commands.md\nindex 69a6000146..ab80601f2d 100644\n--- a/docs/commands.md\n+++ b/docs/commands.md\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ This document provides a comprehensive reference for all Pipenv commands, includ\n \n | Command | Description |\n |---------|-------------|\n+| `init` | Create a Pipfile for a new project, prompting for its settings |\n | `install` | Install packages or create/update virtual environment |\n | `uninstall` | Remove packages from virtual environment and Pipfile |\n | `lock` | Generate Pipfile.lock with dependencies and hashes |\n@@ -23,6 +24,43 @@ This document provides a comprehensive reference for all Pipenv commands, includ\n | `scripts` | List scripts defined in the environment |\n | `open` | Open a Python module in your editor |\n \n+## init\n+\n+The `init` command creates a Pipfile in the current directory by walking you through a short dialog, similar to `npm init`. It asks only about settings a Pipfile records:\n+\n+1. Whether to import packages from a `requirements.txt` in the directory (if one exists)\n+2. The Python version (defaults to the detected interpreter, or `--python`)\n+3. The package index URL (defaults to PyPI, or your pip configuration)\n+4. Packages and dev packages to add, space-separated (e.g. `requests 'flask[async]>=3'`)\n+5. Whether to create the virtualenv and lock right away\n+\n+Project metadata such as name, version and author belongs in `pyproject.toml` and is not part of the dialog.\n+\n+### Options\n+\n+| Option | Description |\n+|--------|-------------|\n+| `-y`, `--yes` | Accept every default without prompting. Implied when stdin is not a terminal. |\n+| `--install` / `--no-install` | Create the virtualenv and lock after writing the Pipfile, or skip it. By default you are asked; with `--yes` it is skipped. |\n+| `--python VERSION` | Python version or interpreter path to record and use. |\n+\n+`init` refuses to overwrite an existing Pipfile in the current directory. A Pipfile in a *parent* directory does not stop it, so you can start a new project inside another one.\n+\n+### Examples\n+\n+```bash\n+# Answer the dialog\n+$ pipenv init\n+\n+# Non-interactive: write a Pipfile with defaults (and import requirements.txt if present)\n+$ pipenv init --yes\n+\n+# Non-interactive, then create the virtualenv and lock\n+$ pipenv init --yes --install --python 3.12\n+```\n+\n+Packages given by path, URL or VCS reference aren't accepted in the dialog; add those afterwards with `pipenv install`.\n+\n ## install\n \n The `install` command is used for installing packages into the Pipenv virtual environment and updating your Pipfile and Pipfile.lock.\ndiff --git a/news/5792.feature.rst b/news/5792.feature.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..c5a31edb32\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/5792.feature.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+Add ``pipenv init``, which creates a Pipfile for a new project through a short dialog (requirements.txt import, Python version, package index, packages and dev packages, and whether to create the virtualenv and lock). ``--yes`` accepts the defaults without prompting, and ``--install`` / ``--no-install`` control the follow-up install. If that install fails, the new Pipfile is removed so ``pipenv init`` can be run again.\ndiff --git a/news/6747.bugfix.rst b/news/6747.bugfix.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..91d413bad0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/6747.bugfix.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+A failed ``pipenv install <package>`` (for example a package that doesn't exist, or a version that can't be resolved) now restores the Pipfile exactly as it was. Previously a lock failure left the new entry in the Pipfile, and a failed upgrade of a package already in the Pipfile could remove that package entirely. An unresolvable dependency also no longer prints a Python traceback after the resolver's error message; pass ``--verbose`` to see it.\ndiff --git a/pipenv/cli/command.py b/pipenv/cli/command.py\nindex bb96a33a1e..1e19801835 100644\n--- a/pipenv/cli/command.py\n+++ b/pipenv/cli/command.py\n@@ -99,6 +99,18 @@ def cmd_install(args, state):\n     do_install(state.project, ctx)\n \n \n+def cmd_init(args, state):\n+    from pipenv.routines.context import RoutineContext\n+    from pipenv.routines.init import do_project_init\n+\n+    ctx = RoutineContext.from_cli(\n+        python=state.python,\n+        pypi_mirror=state.pypi_mirror,\n+        clear=state.clear,\n+    )\n+    do_project_init(state.project, ctx, yes=args.yes, install=args.install)\n+\n+\n def cmd_remove(args, state):\n     from pipenv.utils.virtualenv import cleanup_virtualenv\n \n@@ -635,6 +647,7 @@ def cmd_pylock(args, state):\n \n \n _DISPATCH = {\n+    \"init\": cmd_init,\n     \"install\": cmd_install,\n     \"remove\": cmd_remove,\n     \"upgrade\": cmd_upgrade,\ndiff --git a/pipenv/cli/options.py b/pipenv/cli/options.py\nindex 85ac584f27..2e63810dea 100644\n--- a/pipenv/cli/options.py\n+++ b/pipenv/cli/options.py\n@@ -604,6 +604,31 @@ def build_parser():\n     _add_site_packages_option(p)\n     _add_install_options(p)\n \n+    # \u2500\u2500 init \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n+    p = subs.add_parser(\n+        \"init\",\n+        add_help=False,\n+        help=\"Create a Pipfile for a new project, prompting for its settings.\",\n+    )\n+    p.add_argument(\"-h\", \"--help\", dest=\"help\", action=\"store_true\", default=False)\n+    p.add_argument(\n+        \"-y\",\n+        \"--yes\",\n+        dest=\"yes\",\n+        action=\"store_true\",\n+        default=False,\n+        help=\"Accept all defaults without prompting.\",\n+    )\n+    p.add_argument(\n+        \"--install\",\n+        dest=\"install\",\n+        action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction,\n+        default=None,\n+        help=\"Create the virtualenv and lock after writing the Pipfile \"\n+        \"(default: ask; off with --yes).\",\n+    )\n+    _add_common_options(p)\n+\n     # \u2500\u2500 remove \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     p = subs.add_parser(\n         \"remove\", add_help=False, help=\"Remove the virtualenv for the current project.\"\ndiff --git a/pipenv/routines/init.py b/pipenv/routines/init.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..eb157459ec\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pipenv/routines/init.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+\"\"\"``pipenv init`` \u2014 create a Pipfile for a new project, optionally by dialog.\n+\n+Pipenv manages application environments, not package metadata, so the\n+dialog only asks about things a Pipfile actually records: the Python\n+version, the package index, and the initial packages.  Name / version /\n+author belong in ``pyproject.toml`` and are deliberately out of scope.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import os\n+import shlex\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+from pipenv.patched.pip._vendor.packaging.requirements import (\n+    InvalidRequirement,\n+    Requirement,\n+)\n+from pipenv.patched.pip._vendor.packaging.utils import canonicalize_name\n+from pipenv.patched.pip._vendor.rich.prompt import Confirm, Prompt\n+from pipenv.utils import console, err\n+\n+\n+def parse_package_list(text):\n+    \"\"\"Turn ``\"requests flask>=3 'uvicorn[standard]'\"`` into Pipfile entries.\n+\n+    Returns ``(entries, rejected)`` where ``entries`` maps the canonical\n+    name to a Pipfile entry and ``rejected`` lists the tokens that are\n+    not plain PEP 508 requirements (URLs, paths, editables).  Those still\n+    work with ``pipenv install`` afterwards; they just need the full\n+    install machinery to build a correct Pipfile entry.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    entries = {}\n+    rejected = []\n+    try:\n+        tokens = shlex.split(text)\n+    except ValueError:  # unbalanced quotes\n+        return entries, [text]\n+    for token in tokens:\n+        try:\n+            req = Requirement(token)\n+        except InvalidRequirement:\n+            rejected.append(token)\n+            continue\n+        if req.url:\n+            rejected.append(token)\n+            continue\n+        version = str(req.specifier) or \"*\"\n+        entry = {\"version\": version}\n+        if req.extras:\n+            entry[\"extras\"] = sorted(req.extras)\n+        if req.marker:\n+            entry[\"markers\"] = str(req.marker)\n+        entries[canonicalize_name(req.name)] = (\n+            version if len(entry) == 1 else entry\n+        )\n+    return entries, rejected\n+\n+\n+def _ask(question, default, interactive):\n+    if not interactive:\n+        return default\n+    return Prompt.ask(question, default=default, console=err)\n+\n+\n+def _confirm(question, default, interactive):\n+    if not interactive:\n+        return default\n+    return Confirm.ask(question, default=default, console=err)\n+\n+\n+def _ask_packages(question, interactive):\n+    if not interactive:\n+        return {}\n+    while True:\n+        entries, rejected = parse_package_list(\n+            Prompt.ask(question, default=\"\", show_default=False, console=err)\n+        )\n+        if not rejected:\n+            return entries\n+        err.print(\n+            f\"[yellow]Not a plain requirement: {', '.join(rejected)}.[/yellow] \"\n+            \"Add those afterwards with [bold]pipenv install[/bold].\"\n+        )\n+\n+\n+def _install_or_discard(project, ctx, pipfile_path, do_install):\n+    \"\"\"Run ``do_install``; if it fails, delete the Pipfile ``init`` just wrote.\n+\n+    Otherwise a typo'd or nonexistent package is left in a Pipfile that\n+    blocks re-running ``init``.  ``do_install`` exits via ``SystemExit``\n+    on success too (code 0) and on lock failure (code 1), so a plain\n+    ``except Exception`` would miss the common failure path.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        do_install(project, ctx)\n+    except SystemExit as exc:\n+        if exc.code in (None, 0):\n+            raise\n+        _discard_pipfile(pipfile_path)\n+        raise\n+    except Exception:\n+        _discard_pipfile(pipfile_path)\n+        raise\n+\n+\n+def _discard_pipfile(pipfile_path):\n+    pipfile_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n+    err.print(\n+        f\"[bold red]Installation failed, so {pipfile_path} was removed.[/bold red] \"\n+        \"Fix the problem above and run [bold]pipenv init[/bold] again.\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def do_project_init(project, ctx, yes=False, install=None):\n+    \"\"\"Create a Pipfile in the current directory.\n+\n+    ``yes`` accepts every default without prompting (like ``npm init -y``);\n+    a non-interactive stdin implies it.  ``install`` forces (True) or\n+    skips (False) creating the virtualenv and locking afterwards; ``None``\n+    asks, defaulting to *yes* interactively and *no* under ``--yes``.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    from pipenv.routines.install import do_install\n+\n+    interactive = not yes and sys.stdin.isatty()\n+\n+    # Always initialise in the directory pipenv was invoked from: a Pipfile\n+    # found by the usual parent-directory walk (which Project() has already\n+    # chdir'd into) belongs to some *other* project.\n+    if not project.s.PIPENV_PIPFILE:\n+        os.chdir(project._original_dir)\n+        project.pipfile._location = str(project._original_dir / \"Pipfile\")\n+        project.pipfile._name = None\n+    pipfile_path = Path(project.pipfile.location)\n+    if pipfile_path.exists():\n+        err.print(\n+            f\"[bold red]A Pipfile already exists at {pipfile_path}.[/bold red] \"\n+            \"Use [bold]pipenv install[/bold] to add packages to it.\"\n+        )\n+        sys.exit(1)\n+\n+    # ``--python`` may be an interpreter path or a bare version like\n+    # ``3.12``; create_pipfile only understands the former.\n+    python = ctx.target_env.python\n+    python_path = python if python and Path(python).is_file() else None\n+    project.create_pipfile(python=python_path)\n+\n+    requirements = pipfile_path.parent / \"requirements.txt\"\n+    if requirements.is_file() and _confirm(\n+        f\"Import packages from [bold]{requirements.name}[/bold]?\", True, interactive\n+    ):\n+        from pipenv.utils.dependencies import import_requirements\n+\n+        import_requirements(project, r=str(requirements), replace_default_source=True)\n+\n+    data = project.pipfile.parsed\n+    requires = data.setdefault(\"requires\", {})\n+    current = requires.get(\"python_version\", \"\")\n+    default = python if python and not python_path else current\n+    chosen = _ask(\"Python version\", default, interactive).strip()\n+    if chosen and chosen != current:\n+        requires[\"python_version\"] = \".\".join(chosen.split(\".\")[:2])\n+        if len(chosen.split(\".\")) > 2:\n+            requires[\"python_full_version\"] = chosen\n+        else:\n+            requires.pop(\"python_full_version\", None)\n+\n+    source = data[\"source\"][0]\n+    url = _ask(\"Package index URL\", source[\"url\"], interactive).strip()\n+    if url and url != source[\"url\"]:\n+        source[\"url\"] = url\n+        source[\"verify_ssl\"] = url.startswith(\"https\")\n+\n+    for category, label in ((\"packages\", \"Packages\"), (\"dev-packages\", \"Dev packages\")):\n+        entries = _ask_packages(\n+            f\"{label} [dim](space-separated, blank for none)[/dim]\", interactive\n+        )\n+        data.setdefault(category, {}).update(entries)\n+\n+    project.pipfile.write_toml(data)\n+    console.print(f\"[bold green]Created {pipfile_path}[/bold green]\")\n+\n+    if install is None:\n+        install = interactive and _confirm(\n+            \"Create the virtualenv and lock now?\", True, interactive\n+        )\n+    if install:\n+        _install_or_discard(project, ctx, pipfile_path, do_install)\n+    else:\n+        console.print(\n+            \"Run [bold]pipenv install[/bold] when you're ready to create the \"\n+            \"virtualenv and lock.\"\n+        )\ndiff --git a/pipenv/routines/install.py b/pipenv/routines/install.py\nindex 8be2834213..426d53813a 100644\n--- a/pipenv/routines/install.py\n+++ b/pipenv/routines/install.py\n@@ -348,28 +348,24 @@ def handle_new_packages(\n \n     # Use the update routine for new packages\n     if perform_upgrades and (packages or editable_packages):\n-        try:\n-            # Post T_C.8 ``do_update`` consumes ``RoutineContext``. Build\n-            # a context that mirrors the pre-migration kwargs verbatim\n-            # (dev / pre / packages / editables / pypi_mirror / index /\n-            # extra_pip_args / categories) so the post-install upgrade\n-            # pass behaves identically.\n-            update_ctx = RoutineContext.from_cli(\n-                pypi_mirror=target.pypi_mirror,\n-                pre=policy.pre,\n-                packages=tuple(packages),\n-                editable_packages=tuple(editable_packages),\n-                categories=tuple(pipfile_categories),\n-                dev=sel.dev,\n-                index=index,\n-                extra_pip_args=tuple(extra_pip_args),\n-            )\n-            do_update(project, update_ctx)\n-            return new_packages, True\n-        except Exception:\n-            for pkg_name, category in new_packages:\n-                project.pipfile.remove_package(pkg_name, category)\n-            raise\n+        # Post T_C.8 ``do_update`` consumes ``RoutineContext``. Build\n+        # a context that mirrors the pre-migration kwargs verbatim\n+        # (dev / pre / packages / editables / pypi_mirror / index /\n+        # extra_pip_args / categories) so the post-install upgrade\n+        # pass behaves identically.\n+        update_ctx = RoutineContext.from_cli(\n+            pypi_mirror=target.pypi_mirror,\n+            pre=policy.pre,\n+            packages=tuple(packages),\n+            editable_packages=tuple(editable_packages),\n+            categories=tuple(pipfile_categories),\n+            dev=sel.dev,\n+            index=index,\n+            extra_pip_args=tuple(extra_pip_args),\n+        )\n+        # On failure, do_install restores the Pipfile from its snapshot.\n+        do_update(project, update_ctx)\n+        return new_packages, True\n \n     return new_packages, False\n \n@@ -538,7 +534,6 @@ def do_install(project, ctx: RoutineContext) -> None:\n     sel = ctx.package_selection\n \n     pipfile_categories = list(sel.categories)\n-    new_packages: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n \n     ensure_project(\n         project,\n@@ -557,14 +552,18 @@ def do_install(project, ctx: RoutineContext) -> None:\n \n     do_init(project, ctx)\n \n-    if not policy.deploy:\n-        new_packages, _ = handle_new_packages(\n-            project,\n-            ctx,\n-            perform_upgrades=not policy.skip_lock,\n-        )\n-\n+    # If anything below fails, put the Pipfile back exactly as it was.\n+    # Removing just the \"new\" entries isn't enough: a failed upgrade of an\n+    # existing package would delete it, and lock failures exit through\n+    # SystemExit rather than an Exception.\n+    pipfile_snapshot = project.pipfile.snapshot()\n     try:\n+        if not policy.deploy:\n+            handle_new_packages(\n+                project,\n+                ctx,\n+                perform_upgrades=not policy.skip_lock,\n+            )\n         # When --dev was requested, install both default and dev categories\n         # from the Pipfile (the historical do_install behaviour).\n         install_categories = (\n@@ -577,11 +576,13 @@ def do_install(project, ctx: RoutineContext) -> None:\n             ),\n         )\n         do_install_dependencies(project, deps_ctx, requirements_directory)\n-    except Exception as e:\n-        # If we fail to install, remove the package from the Pipfile.\n-        for pkg_name, category in new_packages:\n-            project.pipfile.remove_package(pkg_name, category)\n-        raise e\n+    except SystemExit as exc:\n+        if exc.code not in (None, 0):\n+            project.pipfile.restore(pipfile_snapshot)\n+        raise\n+    except BaseException:\n+        project.pipfile.restore(pipfile_snapshot)\n+        raise\n \n     sys.exit(0)\n \ndiff --git a/pipenv/routines/lock.py b/pipenv/routines/lock.py\nindex 3faaec4521..ece3fb1097 100644\n--- a/pipenv/routines/lock.py\n+++ b/pipenv/routines/lock.py\n@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@\n import traceback\n from pathlib import Path\n \n+from pipenv.exceptions import ResolutionFailure\n from pipenv.routines.context import RoutineContext\n from pipenv.utils import err\n from pipenv.utils.dependencies import (\n@@ -456,6 +457,12 @@ def do_lock(project, ctx: RoutineContext):\n             )\n         except RuntimeError:\n             sys.exit(1)\n+        except ResolutionFailure:\n+            # The resolver already printed pip's message; a traceback for\n+            # an unresolvable requirement is just noise.\n+            if project.s.is_verbose():\n+                err.print(traceback.format_exc())\n+            sys.exit(1)\n         except Exception:\n             err.print(traceback.format_exc())\n             sys.exit(1)\ndiff --git a/pipenv/utils/pipfile.py b/pipenv/utils/pipfile.py\nindex 678626f03f..cc6ff88896 100644\n--- a/pipenv/utils/pipfile.py\n+++ b/pipenv/utils/pipfile.py\n@@ -886,6 +886,22 @@ def write_toml(self, data, path=None) -> None:\n             self._parsed_cache = None\n             self._parsed_mtime_ns = None\n \n+    def snapshot(self) -> bytes | None:\n+        \"\"\"Return the Pipfile's raw bytes (``None`` if it doesn't exist).\"\"\"\n+        try:\n+            return Path(self.location).read_bytes()\n+        except FileNotFoundError:\n+            return None\n+\n+    def restore(self, content: bytes | None) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Put back exactly what :meth:`snapshot` returned.\"\"\"\n+        if content is None:\n+            Path(self.location).unlink(missing_ok=True)\n+        else:\n+            Path(self.location).write_bytes(content)\n+        self._parsed_cache = None\n+        self._parsed_mtime_ns = None\n+\n     # ---- key lookup / casing --------------------------------------------\n \n     def get_package_name(self, package_name, category):\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/tests/unit/test_do_install_context_routing.py b/tests/unit/test_do_install_context_routing.py\nindex dde2b424f1..115832773f 100644\n--- a/tests/unit/test_do_install_context_routing.py\n+++ b/tests/unit/test_do_install_context_routing.py\n@@ -438,3 +438,33 @@ def test_signature(self):\n             \"procs\",\n             \"requirements_dir\",\n         ]\n+\n+\n+class TestDoInstallRestoresPipfileOnFailure:\n+    \"\"\"A failed install puts the Pipfile back byte-for-byte.\"\"\"\n+\n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+        \"failing, failure\",\n+        [\n+            (\"handle_new_packages\", SystemExit(1)),\n+            (\"handle_new_packages\", RuntimeError(\"boom\")),\n+            (\"do_install_dependencies\", SystemExit(1)),\n+            (\"do_install_dependencies\", KeyboardInterrupt()),\n+        ],\n+    )\n+    def test_failure_restores_snapshot(\n+        self, project_stub, patch_install_pipeline, failing, failure\n+    ):\n+        from pipenv.routines.install import do_install\n+\n+        project_stub.pipfile.snapshot.return_value = b\"original\"\n+        patch_install_pipeline[failing].side_effect = failure\n+        with pytest.raises(type(failure)):\n+            do_install(project_stub, RoutineContext.from_cli(packages=(\"x\",)))\n+        project_stub.pipfile.restore.assert_called_once_with(b\"original\")\n+\n+    def test_success_leaves_pipfile_alone(self, project_stub, patch_install_pipeline):\n+        from pipenv.routines.install import do_install\n+\n+        do_install(project_stub, RoutineContext.from_cli(packages=(\"x\",)))\n+        project_stub.pipfile.restore.assert_not_called()\ndiff --git a/tests/unit/test_init_routine.py b/tests/unit/test_init_routine.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..442a380d9d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/tests/unit/test_init_routine.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@\n+\"\"\"Tests for ``pipenv init`` (``pipenv.routines.init``).\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+from unittest import mock\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from pipenv.routines.context import RoutineContext\n+from pipenv.routines.init import do_project_init, parse_package_list\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    \"text, expected\",\n+    [\n+        (\"\", {}),\n+        (\"requests\", {\"requests\": \"*\"}),\n+        (\"Flask>=3,<4\", {\"flask\": \"<4,>=3\"}),\n+        (\"'Flask>=3' Django==5.1\", {\"flask\": \">=3\", \"django\": \"==5.1\"}),\n+        (\n+            \"uvicorn[standard]>=0.30\",\n+            {\"uvicorn\": {\"version\": \">=0.30\", \"extras\": [\"standard\"]}},\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            \"'pywin32; sys_platform == \\\"win32\\\"'\",\n+            {\"pywin32\": {\"version\": \"*\", \"markers\": 'sys_platform == \"win32\"'}},\n+        ),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_parse_package_list(text, expected):\n+    entries, rejected = parse_package_list(text)\n+    assert entries == expected\n+    assert rejected == []\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    \"token\",\n+    [\"./localpkg\", \"-e .\", \"'pkg @ https://example.com/pkg.whl'\", \"git+https://x/y\", \"'oops\"],\n+)\n+def test_parse_package_list_rejects_non_plain_requirements(token):\n+    entries, rejected = parse_package_list(token)\n+    assert rejected\n+    assert \"pkg\" not in entries\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def project(tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n+    from pipenv.project import Project\n+\n+    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)\n+    monkeypatch.delenv(\"PIPENV_PIPFILE\", raising=False)\n+    monkeypatch.setenv(\"PIPENV_DEFAULT_PYTHON_VERSION\", \"3.12\")\n+    return Project\n+\n+\n+def _ctx(python=None):\n+    return RoutineContext.from_cli(python=python)\n+\n+\n+def test_yes_writes_defaults_and_imports_requirements(project, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"requirements.txt\").write_text(\"six==1.16.0\\n\")\n+    proj = project()\n+    with mock.patch(\"pipenv.routines.install.do_install\") as do_install:\n+        do_project_init(proj, _ctx(), yes=True)\n+\n+    parsed = proj.pipfile.parsed\n+    assert parsed[\"packages\"][\"six\"] == \"==1.16.0\"\n+    assert parsed[\"source\"][0][\"url\"] == proj.default_source[\"url\"]\n+    assert \"python_version\" in parsed[\"requires\"]\n+    do_install.assert_not_called()\n+\n+\n+def test_bare_python_version_is_recorded(project, tmp_path):\n+    proj = project()\n+    do_project_init(proj, _ctx(python=\"3.11\"), yes=True, install=False)\n+    assert proj.pipfile.parsed[\"requires\"][\"python_version\"] == \"3.11\"\n+\n+\n+def test_refuses_existing_pipfile(project, tmp_path):\n+    (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").write_text(\"[packages]\\n\")\n+    with pytest.raises(SystemExit) as exc:\n+        do_project_init(project(), _ctx(), yes=True)\n+    assert exc.value.code == 1\n+\n+\n+def test_parent_pipfile_does_not_block(project, tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n+    (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").write_text(\"[packages]\\n\")\n+    sub = tmp_path / \"sub\"\n+    sub.mkdir()\n+    monkeypatch.chdir(sub)\n+    proj = project()\n+    do_project_init(proj, _ctx(), yes=True, install=False)\n+    assert (sub / \"Pipfile\").is_file()\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").read_text() == \"[packages]\\n\"\n+\n+\n+def test_interactive_dialog(project, tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n+    answers = iter(\n+        [\n+            \"3.11\",  # Python version\n+            \"https://mirror.example/simple\",  # index\n+            \"requests ./local\",  # packages, rejected once\n+            \"requests 'flask[async]>=3'\",  # packages\n+            \"pytest\",  # dev packages\n+        ]\n+    )\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(\"sys.stdin.isatty\", lambda: True)\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(\n+        \"pipenv.routines.init.Prompt.ask\", lambda *a, **k: next(answers)\n+    )\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(\"pipenv.routines.init.Confirm.ask\", lambda *a, **k: True)\n+    proj = project()\n+    with mock.patch(\"pipenv.routines.install.do_install\") as do_install:\n+        do_project_init(proj, _ctx())\n+\n+    parsed = proj.pipfile.parsed\n+    assert parsed[\"requires\"][\"python_version\"] == \"3.11\"\n+    assert parsed[\"source\"][0][\"url\"] == \"https://mirror.example/simple\"\n+    assert parsed[\"packages\"][\"requests\"] == \"*\"\n+    assert parsed[\"packages\"][\"flask\"][\"extras\"] == [\"async\"]\n+    assert parsed[\"dev-packages\"][\"pytest\"] == \"*\"\n+    do_install.assert_called_once()\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"failure\", [SystemExit(1), RuntimeError(\"boom\")])\n+def test_failed_install_removes_new_pipfile(project, tmp_path, failure):\n+    proj = project()\n+    with mock.patch(\n+        \"pipenv.routines.install.do_install\", side_effect=failure\n+    ), pytest.raises(type(failure)):\n+        do_project_init(proj, _ctx(), yes=True, install=True)\n+    assert not (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").exists()\n+\n+\n+def test_successful_install_keeps_pipfile(project, tmp_path):\n+    proj = project()\n+    with mock.patch(\n+        \"pipenv.routines.install.do_install\", side_effect=SystemExit(0)\n+    ), pytest.raises(SystemExit):\n+        do_project_init(proj, _ctx(), yes=True, install=True)\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").is_file()\ndiff --git a/tests/unit/test_pipfile_subsystem.py b/tests/unit/test_pipfile_subsystem.py\nindex bc4a49c1ac..e03531c179 100644\n--- a/tests/unit/test_pipfile_subsystem.py\n+++ b/tests/unit/test_pipfile_subsystem.py\n@@ -396,6 +396,29 @@ def test_remove_packages_bulk_drops_named_entries(project_with_packages):\n     assert \"pytest\" not in parsed.get(\"dev-packages\", {})\n \n \n+@pytest.mark.utils\n+def test_snapshot_restore_round_trips_bytes(project_with_packages, tmp_path):\n+    pipfile = project_with_packages.pipfile\n+    before = (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").read_bytes()\n+    snap = pipfile.snapshot()\n+    assert snap == before\n+    pipfile.remove_package(\"flask\", category=\"packages\")\n+    assert \"flask\" not in pipfile.parsed.get(\"packages\", {})\n+    pipfile.restore(snap)\n+    assert (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").read_bytes() == before\n+    # The parsed cache is dropped, not served stale.\n+    assert \"flask\" in pipfile.parsed[\"packages\"]\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.utils\n+def test_restore_none_removes_pipfile(project_no_pipfile, tmp_path):\n+    pipfile = project_no_pipfile.pipfile\n+    assert pipfile.snapshot() is None\n+    (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").write_text(\"[packages]\\n\")\n+    pipfile.restore(None)\n+    assert not (tmp_path / \"Pipfile\").exists()\n+\n+\n # ---- key lookup / casing --------------------------------------------------\n \n \n", "problem_statement": "Interactive Mode For Pipenv\nWhat if we add an interactive mode to customize virtual environments?\r\nLike what `npm init` does.\r\n```[tasklist]\r\n### Tasks\r\n- [ ] Selection of a colourful library. e.g `rich` or `colorama`\r\n- [ ] Add `-i` and `--interactive` parameters\r\n```\r\n\n", "hints_text": "Both libraries are already included in pipenv.\r\nWhat is exactly the benefit of making our own shell in comparison to using the OS shell?\r\nYou can customize the venv in many ways already:\r\nYou can install packages, set the python version, add variables.\r\nCan you please explain more on what you want to achieve?\r\nPlease also link to the relevant docs of npm.\nI want a prompt interface to customize the project environment. `i.e asks what the name of the project, version, author etc.`\n.I see. What you want is initializing a project with a dialog. That can be done    ", "created_at": "2026-10-18T22:42:11Z"}
{"repo": "pypa/pipenv", "pull_number": 6745, "instance_id": "pypa__pipenv-6745", "issue_numbers": ["5335"], "base_commit": "c8d1faa8562518705fb336e9675f4255a9b81212", "patch": "diff --git a/.pre-commit-config.yaml b/.pre-commit-config.yaml\nindex 6a48acf0a5..2860654b5e 100644\n--- a/.pre-commit-config.yaml\n+++ b/.pre-commit-config.yaml\n@@ -22,6 +22,15 @@ repos:\n   hooks:\n   - id: ruff\n \n+- repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/mirrors-mypy\n+  rev: v2.4.0\n+  hooks:\n+  - id: mypy\n+    # Type-check pipenv's own code only; vendor/ and patched/ are excluded\n+    # in [tool.mypy] and imports into them are skipped (follow_imports).\n+    pass_filenames: false\n+    args: []\n+\n - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/pygrep-hooks\n   rev: v1.10.0\n   hooks:\ndiff --git a/docs/dev/contributing.md b/docs/dev/contributing.md\nindex 08397b1959..f332eabd2d 100644\n--- a/docs/dev/contributing.md\n+++ b/docs/dev/contributing.md\n@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ and install the pre-commit hooks locally:\n    $ pre-commit run --all-files --verbose\n ```\n \n+The pre-commit hooks include [mypy](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/), which type-checks\n+pipenv's own code (`pipenv/vendor/` and `pipenv/patched/` are excluded). Its\n+settings live under `[tool.mypy]` in `pyproject.toml`, so you can also run it\n+directly with `mypy`.\n+\n ### Code Review\n \n Contributions will not be merged until they have been code reviewed. You should\ndiff --git a/news/5335.process.rst b/news/5335.process.rst\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..2c23dcfa7a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/news/5335.process.rst\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+Enable mypy type checking for pipenv's own code (excluding ``pipenv/vendor`` and ``pipenv/patched``) as a pre-commit hook, which also gates CI. Existing type errors were fixed, mostly by correcting annotations and converting legacy ``# type:`` comments to inline annotations.\ndiff --git a/pipenv/cli/options.py b/pipenv/cli/options.py\nindex 15aeb03d86..85ac584f27 100644\n--- a/pipenv/cli/options.py\n+++ b/pipenv/cli/options.py\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@\n import os\n import re\n from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import NoReturn\n \n from pipenv.project import Project\n from pipenv.utils.internet import is_valid_url\n@@ -500,7 +501,7 @@ class _PipenvArgumentParser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n     \"\"\"ArgumentParser subclass that appends 'Did you mean \u2026?' suggestions\n     when the user types an unrecognised subcommand name.\"\"\"\n \n-    def error(self, message: str) -> None:\n+    def error(self, message: str) -> NoReturn:\n         import difflib\n \n         m = re.search(r\"invalid choice: '([^']+)'\", message)\ndiff --git a/pipenv/environment.py b/pipenv/environment.py\nindex df2f6b7287..e0c8f750de 100644\n--- a/pipenv/environment.py\n+++ b/pipenv/environment.py\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@\n \n if typing.TYPE_CHECKING:\n     from types import ModuleType\n-    from typing import ContextManager, Generator\n+    from typing import Any, Generator, Iterator\n \n     from pipenv.project import Project, TPipfile, TSource\n     from pipenv.vendor import tomlkit\n@@ -54,10 +54,10 @@\n class Environment:\n     def __init__(\n         self,\n-        prefix: str | None = None,\n+        prefix: str | Path | None = None,\n         python: str | None = None,\n         is_venv: bool = False,\n-        base_working_set: list[importlib_metadata.Distribution] = None,\n+        base_working_set: Iterable[importlib_metadata.Distribution] | None = None,\n         pipfile: tomlkit.toml_document.TOMLDocument | TPipfile | None = None,\n         sources: list[TSource] | None = None,\n         project: Project | None = None,\n@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ def __init__(\n         super().__init__()\n         self._modules = {\"pipenv\": pipenv}\n         self.base_working_set = base_working_set if base_working_set else BASE_WORKING_SET\n-        prefix = normalize_path(prefix)\n+        prefix = normalize_path(prefix if prefix else sys.prefix)\n         self._python = None\n         if python is 