ro\\.venv\\lib\\site-packages\\pipenv\\patched\\pip\\_vendor\\requests\\sessions.py\", line 706, in send\n    r = adapter.send(request, **kwargs)\n  File \"C:\\temp\\pipenv-repro\\.venv\\lib\\site-packages\\pipenv\\patched\\pip\\_vendor\\cachecontrol\\adapter.py\", line 76, in\nsend\n    resp = super().send(request, stream, timeout, verify, cert, proxies)\n  File \"C:\\temp\\pipenv-repro\\.venv\\lib\\site-packages\\pipenv\\patched\\pip\\_vendor\\requests\\adapters.py\", line 676, in send\n    raise SSLError(e, request=request)\npipenv.patched.pip._vendor.requests.exceptions.SSLError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='pypi.org', port=443): Max retries\nexceeded with url: /pypi/idna/json (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED]\ncertificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1007)')))\n\nPS C:\\temp\\pipenv-repro>\n````\n\n</details>\n\n### Root cause (analyzed against `main` @ 2026.7.1)\n\n`pipenv lock`'s hash-lookup session is built by `get_requests_session()` (`pipenv/utils/internet.py`). This session loads no certificates other than whatever `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` points to. If `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` is set to a file containing only one additional CA (e.g. for a proxy or a private index), this session cannot verify any host whose certificate isn't covered by that file \u2014 including unrelated public infrastructure such as `pypi.org` \u2014 and fails.\n\n### Steps to replicate\n\n1. Create a CA certificate that does not cover `pypi.org` (stands in for \"`REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` = one additional/private CA only\"):\n\n```powershell\n$cert = New-SelfSignedCertificate -DnsName \"dummy-ca\" `\n    -CertStoreLocation \"Cert:\\CurrentUser\\My\" -KeyUsage CertSign -NotAfter (Get-Date).AddYears(1)\nExport-Certificate -Cert $cert -FilePath \"dummy-ca.cer\" | Out-Null\ncertutil -encode \"dummy-ca.cer\" \"dummy-ca.pem\" | Out-Null\n```\n\n2. Point `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` at it and run `pipenv lock` in a project with any `Pipfile` that has a package pinned (e.g. `requests = \"*\"`):\n\n```powershell\n$env:REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE = \"$PWD\\dummy-ca.pem\"\npipenv lock -v\n```\n\n`pipenv lock` fails with `SSLCertVerificationError`.\n\n### Related reports\n\nFor reference, similar reports exist:\n\n- #4314 \u2014 a comment traced the failure to pipenv's hash-lookup session during `lock`, with a workaround of adding the custom CA into the interpreter's own `certifi` `cacert.pem`.\n- #5665 \u2014 comment-thread discussion traced the same symptom to pipenv's lock-time hash-lookup session.\n\nProbably shouldn't be advising me to use deprecated arguments\nBe sure to check the existing issues (both open and closed!), and make sure you are running the latest version of Pipenv.\n\nCheck the [diagnose documentation](https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/diagnose.html) for common issues before posting! We may close your issue if it is very similar to one of them. Please be considerate, or be on your way.\n\nMake sure to mention your debugging experience if the documented solution failed.\n\n\n### Issue description\n\npipenv suggests that I `--rm` my environment, and then when I go to execute that command, I'm admonished for using a soon to be deprecated flag/command.\n\n### Expected result\n\nSuggest I run The Current Thing(tm)\n\n### Actual result\n\n```\n$ pipenv shell\nWarning: Your Pipfile requires \"python_version\" 3, but you are using 3.14.6 from\n/home/j/.local/share/v/r/bin/python.\n$ pipenv --rm and rebuilding the virtual environment may resolve the issue.\n$ pipenv check will surely fail.\nLaunching subshell in virtual environment...\n\n__PIPENV_SHELL_READY__\n$ exit\n$ pipenv --rm\nWarning: --rm is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. Use `pipenv remove` instead.\nRemoving virtualenv (/home/jasmerb/.local/share/virtualenvs/reflog-gOwc5Loq)...\n$\n```\n\n### Steps to replicate\n\nProvide the steps to replicate (which usually at least includes the commands and the Pipfile).\n\n---------